    92	## Fragment prompts, refusals and uses
    93	
    94	- **The eleventh (*This far?*):** asks of the ladder's head (291st), of the handcart's tail-board, of the bar on the carts' street, of each landing, of the round of the lamp, of the groove at the blue gate (where it asks hardest and is told no), of the ring on a threshing floor it never sees. Told no every time. Deployment: none.
    95	- **The twelfth:** comes at the word; shows the fifth row and the board; then leans at the table's edge, the desk, the stair's treads, the handcart's wheel, three hundred yards of rope-walk (one look he did not mean: a grain of a bill), the bridge (not looked at), the lamp-ring, the inn table (caught late), the dividers' hinge (caught late), the leaf (kept shut: "this was hers"). Never a person. Never the crown. Never himself.
    96	- **Shadow:** lifts at dusk each day and is told no; on the night of the tail it stands at his knees for three hours and is told no at the rope-walk, at the tar yard and at the wicket. Twice in all and sealed.
    97	- **Wind (*Away?*), the read (*What does it weigh?*), Anchor (*There?*), Pressure, Ember:** each asks once in the tail and is told no. **Compression** comes into his heels on the stair when the old man's weight shifts, and is told to wait. **Tide:** unused; no self-reading.
    98	- **Counted uses in the movement: none.** Deployment since the Line at movement end: thirty-two. Fragments at movement end: twelve.
