    96	## 3. The expansion plan — where the extra ≈197,000 words come from
    97	
    98	Nothing below may change an end state, move a death, add an acquisition, or disclose a reserved truth early (§11). Every new episode must fit the sequence locks in §13. Word figures are planning estimates, not quotas.
    99	
   100	### A. Fights and set pieces given developed room (≈46,000)
   101	
   102	| Fight / set piece | Source | Edition allowance | Why |
   103	|---|---|---|---|
   104	| **The cut** (stillhounds; Iron Wall's first showing) | S4, ~1,800 | 3,500–4,000 plus a scouting scene | Iron Wall's limit must be taught here (rooted, loud, the man is the plane's foot) before the alley pays it off. The crew's silent doctrine is re-taught to a man who has only ever stood. |
   105	| **The alley** (the stepped cut, six faceless) | S12, ~2,400 | 4,000 | The corridor rewards the wall the road punished. Cael learns "being the reason" from inside it. The acquisition minute needs its long, quiet middle. |
   106	| **The Span** (watch-post; barricade; width) | S19, ~2,600 | 4,500 | Force must be witnessed for a full exchange. The width tactic is invented live and fairly priced: nothing is gained inside the line. |
   107	| **The pass** (rig; seven volleys; the death) | S21, ~3,800 | 5,500 | This is the book's costliest fight. The terrain causes two beats (the fall, the swept scree). The young one's death must be prepared and not gratuitous. Force's first use is paid in the ribs. |
   108	| **NEW — The shale-back herd at the axe-head fence** (cold weather) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | summarized as "we walked the fence" | 3,000 | A cold-weather set piece [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] needing no Path: a herd of armoured grazers sheltering on the fence line's slope must be moved without stampeding them ("lethal on a slope when herded wrong"). It teaches the Iron read on frozen ground, Lira benched by her sling, Seln's posts, and Brom reading a line. |
   109	| **NEW — The ice road** (161st) | one line | 3,000 | A carter's cart goes through the river-ice. Cael, Brom and Seln haul it out without declaring, reading load on the ice. The fragments are taught as practical knowledge. It pays later at the cut's frozen runnel. |
   110	| **NEW — The silent yard** (cold-weather learning bouts with Teague's crew) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | absent | 3 bouts × ~1,500 = 4,500 | No Paths, steel and bodies only, in the frozen meadow. Cael loses to the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59]'s spear reach (she never speaks), then corrects. One-armed Lira coaches from the bench. The rival clock appears on the page. This must not touch the sequence locks in §13 (no wall drill; Seln teaches nobody). |
   111	| **NEW — Lira's return to the floor** (270th–276th) | absent | 2,000 | Her first two-armed bout since the Ring, against Cael. The arm "tells her" once and she does not stop. That is a visible correction, and it pays at Millrace ("Once."). |
   112	| **NEW — The ferry's first landing** (277th, high water) | quiet landing | 1,500 | Rope and flood. Vastin is seen holding a physical line, with no Path, before anyone knows it is him. Iron Wall must not show before the cut. |
   113	| **NEW — The tail in Treswick** (291st–292nd) | absent | 2,500 | After the alley, Seln and Cael tail a hood through the outer district at night. The hood passes through a tier gate Cael cannot legally cross. The faction stays faceless and unlocated, and the promise and the bar become physical. |
   114	| **NEW — Water at the seep** (301st–302nd, dry camps) | "two camps with no water" | 3,000 | The two crews must water themselves and a mule at a seep where shale-backs stand on a slope. Teague's field captaincy is shown. The young one moves too fast and the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59] stops him with a hand. That is his habit, set up for the pass. |
   115	| **Lesser exchanges given their beats** | — | ~4,500 | The alley's aftermath; the Span's broad-man fall; the ridge recovery of the mule; the court's pacing as a physical task. |
   116	
   117	### B. Learning and training arcs (≈30,000)
   118	
   119	1. **Cael's working inventory during the cold term** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (≈6,000; first third). Through private practice in the ferryman's shed and the frozen meadow, the reader learns all ten fragments as costs and limits. Wind's burst and its locked landing beat. Pressure's narrow channel. The Iron read as "the workhorse". Compression's frame. Ember, one point at a time, with its burn (used at the Ring and the Stair in Book 7). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] Shadow's idle draw and the seal's logic. Storm, its lanes and their bills (ten / ten / twelve) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling]. Anchor used both ways. Blade, short and sharp. Tide "ask first"; he has read himself three times and Oryn twice, each outward use after an ask and explicit yes. **Invent no new numeric ceilings. Preserve every numeric ceiling and bill fixed by canon.** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]
   120	2. **The kit and the cord** (≈3,000). Karis teaches the crew to pace with the cord. The anomaly is discovered **as a scene** on the 168th, not as a log line.
   121	3. **Vastin learning the crew's doctrine and "to be nobody"** (≈5,000, distributed). Day one of the border road is a silent-movement drill: walk silent, signal by hand, nobody declares unless meant to be loud. Then the cut's lesson, the spring's "Draft nothing", the yard door's "Be nobody", his week of moving toward the lamp and stopping (four times, then two), and the first order he takes and keeps (Millrace).
   122	4. **The Deepstacks decipherment** (≈8,000). The chamber days 285–292 are put on the page, including the undramatized 288th–289th. Cleon's method (bones before words), the board's numerals, Karis's letters coming one at a time from the three floors, and the lamp's discipline. Karis refuses to guess. **The leaf must not become readable on the page before the seventh day** (§13).
   123	5. **Rune practice and cost** (≈3,000). After the 291st Cael catches himself reading made things everywhere: the inn table's joints, the bridge's arches, the dividers' hinge. He learns that the eyes pay, and pays it in the dark (Millrace). It is never used on a person. He does not turn it on himself until it turns unbidden.
   124	6. **Force, dry** (≈2,000). On the shale step (305th) he lines his frame without firing. The thirteenth "listens" and the ribs warn him. The first actual use comes at the pass.
   125	7. **Lira's arm** (≈3,000). The rehab runs from the release to Millrace's "an arm": grip work, the floor-testing rise, the left hand into the coat and out to check it moves, and two arms used on the scree at the cut.
   126	
   127	### C. Summarized events put on the page (≈46,000)
   128	
   129	- **The cold months (131st–264th)** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The cold-term board [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
   130	- **The week before the ferry (270th–276th)** (≈4,000). Tents return to the meadow. Teague's crew prepares for the road after the thaw. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Oryn's first Lowmarch stop: patients at the plank, seen from the outside.
   131	- **Treswick's days** (≈8,000). The outer district as a mechanism: brokers' tally boards, the smith's two forges, the ring road at night. The undramatized chamber days.
   132	- **The 294th: the list of parts** (≈2,000). Copying all day, Cleon's finger on the last line, and his correction "Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line".
   133	- **The road east (295th–297th)** (≈5,000). Each halt read backwards. The cut revisited. "Known".
   134	- **The leg (299th–303rd)** (≈9,000). The Stair's bowl rim, where Karis checks a number for an hour. The cairn: Oryn chooses east. The Hall's marsh, where Cael read himself twice earlier at the Hall. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Two dry camps. Two crews learning each other. The crest at dusk.
   135	- **The court's pacing** (≈2,000). The pacing, about fifty cords [M1 audit: not 159], with Lira on the line and the count spoken.
   136	- **The burial and the mule** (≈2,000).
   137	
   138	### D. Supporting-cast arcs — ten people, many small beats each (≈40,000 including cutaways)
   139	
   140	| Person | Private want | Independent decisions this book (on the page) | Small beats (target count) |
   141	|---|---|---|---|
   142	| **Lira** | To find out what she is without a ladder | Asks Oryn to mend the ankle (her first ask since Norhold). Fights on through the arm's first warning (M2), then listens at the second. Keeps her registry paper in her coat and goes up as a hand. Looks at the whole ladder and it does not pull. Holds her question at the court ("Well?") and accepts "on the road". | 12 |
   143	| **Brom** | Worth without a number | Prices Vastin at three hundred miles. Takes the cart's weight on the good shoulder and pays for it. Declines the broker's post by picking up the box. Says "Good" to Cleon. Carries at Teague's leave. | 10 |
   144	| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
   145	| **Seln** | To keep his old life undecided and his own | Tells only Brom about the posts. Sets the sheet before Cael without a word. Teaches Vastin the first thing he ever teaches anyone. Truthful deflection at the yard door. Walks the tiers and decides nothing. Keeps the cache "a while longer". Climbs the swept scree. | 10 |
   146	| **Oryn** | The route; to be nobody's recruit | Releases the arm only when Lira lifts the sling herself. Comes to Lowmarch unasked. Sets the station term in the log. Routes north. Rejoins as a stop. Asks every time. Walks on east at the cairn. Will not hear the leaf at her table. Turns north "the day I have to". | 11 |
   147	| **Vastin** | To dig one thing up before he's done; to learn to navigate without authority | Walks three hundred miles alone. Carries the case unasked. Consents to be counted as a hand. Holds the wall with nothing behind it. Asks for the wall to be entered. Does not name the seals. Takes Oryn's order. Does not ask to join. | 14 |
   148	| **Cleon** | The work finished and believed, without leaving the Deepstacks | Sets terms at noon. Shows the inside of the Path to no one before Karis. Refuses to finish the sentence. Looks away from the boy deliberately. Comes up the stair once. | 6 |
   149	| **Teague** | To be at the front of the thing; to keep his people | Holds the after-thaw term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Names the contract's terms. Goes through the middle. Does not turn when the broad man falls. Does not put his three across the court's line. Carries the letter. | 7 |
   150	| **Pike** | An honest ledger | Prices the cold term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Prices Vastin at nothing yet. Leaves the season line blank, then dates it. | 4 |
   151	| **The young one** (Teague's; unnamed; his name is never written) [OWNER-pending #54] | To be counted as crew, not the boy with the cloth | Carries the cloth. Volunteers at the seep and is stopped. Steps over the iron when Teague looks at him ("Four"). Nods with his whole head. Goes to the broad man. | 5 |
   152	
   153	The tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59], the broad man and the older healer get two or three beats each, inside Teague's arc. **Keep every member of Teague's crew unnamed** (canon: "keep unnamed unless a later card needs one"; never invent a name for an existing role).
   154	
   155	### E. New episodes inside canon (≈23,000; most are counted under A above)
   156	
   157	The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
   158	
   159	### F. Humour and warmth (≈12,000, distributed; no quota)
   160	
   161	Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
