    26	  - `STATE_LEDGER.md`, latest section.
    27	
    28	## Where we enter
    29	
    30	It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
    31	
    32	## What this movement is for
    33	
    34	The book turns east, on the same road read backwards. Two crews join by contract and not by friendship. Cael watches the Force line in a meadow and does not yet know where it will matter. The grade is cracked, and the sites run oldest-last into the deep edge. At Millrace the healer reads him as deep as she goes. Meanwhile, and against the card, the second instrument turns inward by itself. We are in the last third now: progression surfaces at turning points, and the grade's vocabulary is counted separately (§7.2).
    35	
    36	Consequential turns and promises:
    37	- **The list of parts and the goodbye (294th).** "Your hand's better than mine on the fourth line." At the iron door: **"Work. Not a finding."** / **"Mind the stair. It leans."**
    38	- **The road east (295th–297th; ~5,000).** On the bridge he counts five piers, and does not look at the crown. The spring, with the wind in their faces this time. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited:** "Here." Vastin puts his weight on the knee with the stick off the ground, once. "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted" (Cael's). The feeling of being *known* is entered under each date.
    39	- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
    40	- **Force seen (298th morning).** The meadow cart. The frame lined up heel to palm, a body's length. The wrist clicks, and the young one's cloth is ready. "Don't put it in front of anything that needs doing twice." Cael enters the line and its cost.
    41	- **The grade cracked (298th morning).** Teague is at the door for the dividers, not the marks. There are three marks; the box for the first tier is ruled and never used. Cleon's list puts the kindling mark and the sheet mark in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point falls past the fourth, in the straightedge's shadow. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation … Not what it means." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." **The log, verbatim** (the grandmother is *Cael's*: §12 C4).
    42	- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
    43	- **The deep reading (~3,000).** "May I?" / "Yes." It is the long one. Her current goes round the place. **The twelfth turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** It is not named, and he keeps the check out of his wrist and the change out of his face. The eyes pay in the dark. **Oryn's finding, verbatim.** He withholds his own and enters his reasons in order. Lira offers the leaf. "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf …" / "Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."
    44	- **Dawn (299th).** Twelve and a mule. The pencil line runs from the fourth circle onto the blank sheet and past the divider's point.
    45	
    46	**Physical challenge:** the road and the cut walked again on a bad knee. Force seen. As a learning encounter, the two crews work together in the Lowmarch meadow, **silent movement and march order only. They do not drill under a wall** (§13).
    47	**Cutaway (~2,500):** Teague. He sets the contract's terms before the plank, and thinks about why he is going (to be at the front of the thing). The wrist. The young one. **He knows nothing of the mechanism.**
    48	**Development:** about 14 Cael beats. Supporting: Karis 2, Oryn 2, Vastin 2, Teague 2, Lira 1, Brom 1, the young one 1, Pike 1.
    49	
    50	## What must remain true / withheld
    51	
    52	- **Force is seen, not acquired.** The thirteenth comes at the Span's barricade.
    53	- The Rune finding is **told to no one**. Oryn's finding is hers, whole. The two instruments' disagreement stays unresolved.
    54	- Oryn does **not** hear the leaf. Cleon is not above ground; his goodbye is at the iron door.
    55	- The grade is observation only, with no who and no why. No first-tier site appears. "Four hundred years" occurs only in the fixed 298th log.
    56	- "Noted" order: Vastin's first is here. Teague does not say it yet.
    57	- The wall's count is the crew's six, Karis included, plus Teague's four. The healers are not on it.
    58	
    59	## What the author owns
    60	
    61	How the road east reads in reverse. The plank room's crowd. The meadow's details. Teague's crew at the table. How the grade's numbers come off the sheets. Millrace's lean-to, light and noise. How long the deep reading takes on the page.
    62	
    63	## Where we leave pressure
    64	
    65	Twelve walk east along a straightedge's line, two of them on no wall's count. A healer's route and a researcher's archive ride on one mule. A boy carries two findings that do not agree and a warning that has started to lean. Five days out is a fence the Compact built, and somebody is still watching it.

