    33	19. **The chronicle.** A second leaf from the bundle, paper, in the old town's ink hand, which Karis reads at sight. One line, whole, placed, read as far as a hole a thumb wide. "Marked." (Karis) / "Marked." (Cleon), placed. A slip laid in it. No gloss by anybody, the narration included.
    34	20. **Vastin reaches.** His sentence is given only as its stopped end ("… the mark that is given at the kindling —"): MARKER. Karis: two pages, in few words, and the ruler line, whole (Tier B), placed. He names what he was doing (drafting) and stops.
    35	21. **The copy.** Karis writes the leaf out fair, once; the Tier A 3 line is placed as she writes it, with the gap ruled as a small empty box. Lira and Brom come back. "Tonight. On paper."
    36	22. **Vastin (cutaway; two scenes; the afternoon and the stair).** *Aimed.* He goes over imperfect, then designed (his Book 6 line, whole, in memory), then the third word. He goes over what he signed. His sentence about the mark stays stopped in his own head: he puts it down each time it rises, by the rule a small grey man gave him at a spring. No sigils, no plates, no dates, no seals named. He asks for a quarter-hour's start on the stair and takes it alone, backward, in the dark.
    37	23. **The 293rd evening.** At the bell Cleon lets the sheets lie one night more (mine, to meet the next packet's 294th; flagged). Karis gives Cael the copy to carry. At the stair's head, by the lamp, he reads its first line and finds it the right way up: nobody is on the other side of it (the §13 lock: "somewhere on Treswick's stair"). On the carts' street Seln is told: "Made." / "For a kind." are whole but neither speaker is pinned: MARKER. Karis has told Cleon the house; he has said that he does not come up.
    38	24. **The yard fire.** An iron fire-basket by the stable door, since one of them cannot climb. Cleon comes in under the arch by the yard, the only time; an eighth bowl. Fixed order. **Lira first:** Cael gives her the page; nobody explains it; her line (Tier A 17, hers, whole) is placed. **The circle:** Brom prices it (what it cost to build, and that a price is not a verdict); Seln: "… a while longer" is a phrase only: MARKER; Karis says two pages and falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." (placed; the set-up is mine: Cleon says that the leaf stays under his hand and goes to no counter). **Vastin:** his three-part speech is elided: MARKER; the exchange with Lira: her line, "I did.", "His?" placed; "No. I read it, after. I did not sign it." … "I would have." elided: MARKER; "Yes," Lira said. "You would have." placed. **Cael,** on his feet, not catalogued: the pole-two speech is elided: MARKER; Lira's "Yeah." … "Now what." elided: MARKER; his answer elided: MARKER. Cleon leaves: "Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts." (placed). The log that night has the count and nothing of what he said.
