    96	The launch prompt lists the leaf, Cleon's warning and pole two among units to be placed whole. As BOOK_MAP §10 prints them, each carries an elision; by the same prompt's rule (and Movement 5's practice, where an elision hid two spoken sentences) I have left each as one marker rather than set the pieces with joins of my own. If the coordinator holds that these are whole as given, the pieces can be dropped into the marker's place without touching the scene round it.
