   343	The old woman was over the line before the child's knees had begun to go. They did go, a little. She was caught, and held, with a grey head bent to hers. Oryn, on a bench forty yards off, saw the girl's mouth move against her grandmother's ear, three or four words, quick, and saw the old arms tighten.
