     2	
     3	She had found it on the seventh day, and she did not say so until the eighth, because a thing found on paper is a thing you read three times before you say it once, and she had read it twice by lamplight in a hole under a city, and a third time at first light, with a man beside her who had had a piece of it for ten years and had said nothing while she read, which was, Cael understood afterward, all that the man had left to give.
