    24	
    25	She read it as she read everything, at the size of a finding, and slowly, because it was a thing written in a hand centuries dead in a language the Compact had never converted, and she was reading it through a board and a floor and ten years of a man's notes, and she gave every word its own weight and did not give any word more than its own, and Cael held the lamp still and listened as the cataloguer listens, which is to the words and not to what they are about.
    26	
