    43	She did not say the third word to anyone. She said it to the leaf, in the small voice, the one she kept for the finding she had wished to be wrong about, and Cael understood that she had chosen the word on the stair that morning and had carried it down and had put it at the end so that it would be the last thing said and not the first, and that she had put it there because it was the true one and because she was Karis, and Karis did not put a true thing anywhere but where it went.
