    65	She drew a second leaf toward her — not from the bundle; from a different place on the table, a thing on its own square of cloth, smaller, of the same horn-coloured stuff but thinner and more broken, with its edges gone to crumbs and a hole through its middle the size of a thumb, so that what was on it was two-thirds of what had been.
