    53	Not the stillness of a man being nobody. The other one — the one Cael had seen on a rim and a landing and in a lane: the stillness of a man who has just heard a thing that is about him, and has understood that it is about him, and has not yet decided what his face is going to do, and has forty years of practice at not letting a face decide before the man does. The Compact's own held line, standing in a hole under a Compact registry, hearing a leaf read. He did not move. He did not draft anything. He stood with the stillness on him like a coat, and Cael looked at him and looked away, because that was Vastin's, and it was not this morning's, and the man knew it.
