universe/STATE_LEDGER.md:172:**Calendar:** the book runs from the forty-sixth day past the Line (Ch1, Lowmarch) to the hundred and thirtieth (Ch24, the ferry's last run). Fixed dates the later books must honor: the Fallow Ring entered and Lira's arm bitten on the 96th; the Thornwater circle ("we find the others, all of them") on the 110th; Millrace rendezvous on the 113th; the Long Stair 114th–115th (the trap on the rim on the 114th; the floor and the kit, and the straightedge used at the rim, on the 115th); the Drowned Hall 116th–119th, then two days' rest at the marsh (119th–120th); the fourth site sighted and paced from outside at dusk on the 123rd; Lowmarch and first snow on the 129th. **Cael is eighteen at Ch1 and turns nineteen on the page in Ch14.** (Bibles' Arc 3 age band of 20–22 is now contradicted by drafted prose in B6–B7; reconcile arc-wide in the bible pass — do not retrofit prose.)
