editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:14:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:16:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 4 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Who is where on the 284th:** inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat and the hide; Cleon let them in, counted loads and not people, and shut the door. The unnamed yard clerk is outside; **Seln is above ground, NOT on the card or the count**, watching who comes to the door. Oryn is two gates north with the brown mule. (2) **The count:** Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands, entered by count; the clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written anywhere; the asset-restriction is still pending. Cards are good only for the day written on them and are torn at each gate; Iron passes the second wall and Bronze the third by right, on a certificate that is read out and written. The way to the registry's yard is the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window**; it never crosses the square. Cael has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; Lira keeps the same discipline unasked. (3) **Cleon's terms** (given at the cook-house on the 283rd): all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is never said aloud by him); **nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one drawn sheet and knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets, older than what the Compact found; he has not noticed Cael. **His Path has not been shown.** "Rune Path. Bronze." is all that is known of it, from Seln. (4) **Cael:** ten fragments; deployment thirty-two; the fourth and fifth self-readings were made on the 281st, round the still place and not in, uncounted; Tide feels only what flows and returned nothing ("a cord on a stone… *no length*"); he needs an instrument for what does not move, and owes Oryn the telling at the mill. Lira has read the log. (5) **Vastin and Cael:** Vastin has told him why he declined the second reading (the Ostrand case, causal; and a private relief at never learning what a plate would say); Cael has told him that the place was read twice and returned nothing, and nothing of what reads. Ground, not friendship. Vastin carries three sheets under one seal that he will not show; he has sat three times; his right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th (stick; no kneeling, running or wall) and he caught a slip on the steps with his left hand. Brom's two toes: five days left on the 284th. Lira's arm: day nineteen out of wool; her registry paper unshown; the ladder did not pull. (6) **The inn:** the long loft over the stable, by the yard half-door (the painted door has a book), for a week from the 282nd, pot at dusk, seven bowls; **purse 136 marks**. The outer gate counts feet on a bead-frame and writes no name. (7) **Stone:** the grey bridge, the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the iron door's frame are one dark dry-laid stone older than the walls; Karis has seen it and stated no conclusion beyond "the bridge was first". The iron door has no lock or handle outside; the clerk knocks. (8) The sixty yards of four-strand were priced at the rope-walk and are to be bought going out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:18:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 5 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two; purse 134 marks** at the end of Movement 5 (the night of the 290th). The eleventh, Iron-Wall-adjacent, came from Vastin in the alley's quiet minute; it did not fill, it *set*; its prompt is *This far?*; it has not been deployed and **Vastin has not been told** (Cael holds that as a debt he cannot yet pay; Lira has read the log). (2) **How acquisition lines are printed in this book:** the protected "Fragment eleven" and "Fragment twelve" units are CAEL'S OWN cataloguing of what he reads — set once, in italics, framed as his plain words; they are NOT printed as a system block and take no FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading or code fence. (3) **The Deepstacks:** an iron door with a sliding bar inside; twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine; three galleries. Middle gallery about 110 strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at its end, a shelf above it with a jar, a tied bundle ("Paper. Not stone.") and the black oak plank's sacking; the fifty-two sheets on three tables, 11/29/12; the plank stands against the third table. Eastern gallery: the old town's tall tally-books. One CARRIED lamp, Cleon's, held "a hand to the left" (Cael holds it and has begun to put it where the eyes are about to go). The boxes go up at the clerk's bell and come down each morning on a fresh card; the clerk writes *The same* and *four*. (4) **Cleon** knows Karis's name (he heard Brom say it and has used it once); his own is on the card and has never been said aloud. He has shown his Path from OUTSIDE only (bear / carried / nothing; "They're orders."; "Same make."; the limit: it does not work on a river, a man or a tree, and costs his eyes for an hour). **His week runs from the 287th to the 293rd.** He has not noticed Cael and knows nothing of the alley or the mechanism. (5) **Karis** has fourteen of twenty-three letters and reads numbers and number-words only; seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing; the bundle is tied and unread; Vastin's copied page is in her coat, unshown to Cleon. Her LEFT palm has seven stitches of Brom's under a strip of his shirt; she writes with the right. (6) **Vastin:** his right knee went again in the alley on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty (a wall on it against her order, which he heard and asks that she be told); re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He gave his name, rank and office aloud at the yard hatch on the 285th; nothing of it was written. He still knows nothing of what Cael carries. (7) **Brom:** the left (good) shoulder wrenched under a dray on the 286th and worse after the alley; he carries his box on the bound right shoulder, a debt entered for the mill's healers; the broker's offer (a guard's post inside the second wall) was answered "I'll think on it." and declined in fact. Lira: day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th; a bruised right shoulder; she drops from heights without the arm. (8) **Seln:** a registry clerk knows his face and voice (the price of a truthful answer at the hatch); he watches from the roof above the cut. His case is **SHUT** — never "unopened" (this edition's Book 6 opened it for the five) — and its contents are named nowhere in this book. He has seen one watcher three times (horseman's boots with the spur-rests cut away). (9) **The faction** (six, hooded, no faces, no Path opened) knows the loft and has shown that it knows; it saw Vastin's wall, a rock, a knife and a boy who stood still, and nothing of quiet ground or the fragments. Cael has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again. The loft is paid to the 295th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30:It is the 294th day. The list of parts takes all day, and Cleon's finger is on the last line at the bell. Twelve fragments. Karis's hand is bound and she writes with it anyway. Vastin is on day 15 of a month. There is still no mule.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:39:- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- **The deep reading (~3,000).** "May I?" / "Yes." It is the long one. Her current goes round the place. **The twelfth turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** It is not named, and he keeps the check out of his wrist and the change out of his face. The eyes pay in the dark. **Oryn's finding, verbatim.** He withholds his own and enters his reasons in order. Lira offers the leaf. "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf …" / "Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."
