editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:55:## #35 — B4 month arithmetic (coordinator flag, 2026-10-05; extends C8 / BOOK_MAP §11)
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:56:The edition's Book 4 calendar (closed M4: the Fiske bout ≈d141, Fiske's protected "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final.") puts the eleventh of Sowing (Cael's birthday, ≈d167) about sixteen days before the Copper final and the semester evaluation, which the plan dates in Reaping (inspection from "the twelfth day of Reaping"; the evaluation "the twentieth of Reaping"). Sixteen days cannot span from an eleventh to a nineteenth/twentieth of a different, ordinary-length month.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:57:**DEFAULT in force:** the prose never states month lengths, which month follows which, or a day count between a Sowing date and a Reaping date; day counts are stated only in days/weeks from events. The protected Sowing/Reaping dates stand. Owner may later rule the series calendar (e.g. Reaping as the month after Sowing with a shorter feast-month between, or moving the birthday earlier). Does not block.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:59:**#35 update (coordinator, 2026-10-05, B4 M5 review).** The plan's own protected lines collided: M4's "Six weeks. I'll see you in the final." (closed, published) vs the M5 closing Log's "Semester evaluation in nine weeks." Ruling: the Log now reads "seventeen days" (BOOK_MAP §9 amended). With the final on the nineteenth of Reaping and the evaluation on the twentieth, M6–M7's events fit the seventeen days (semifinal ≈ the tenth, nine days before the final; delegation the twelfth/thirteenth). The one residue is the birthday's month name: "the eleventh of Sowing" falls about sixteen days before the nineteenth of Reaping. The DEFAULT above stands (never state month order or a cross-month day count). Owner options: accept short months / an intercalary feast-week; or move the birthday to "the third of Reaping" (B5's recollection would follow).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:66:4. **Season.** B3 ch1:136 says "Early autumn"; ch9 says the Reydan entry reached Karis "in the first days of autumn". The B2 map says "name no months; keep departure before hard winter", and the B2 M8 draft has frost on the departure morning and "before the first snow". **Default:** B2 ch60's departure morning names no season and shows no frost or snow. Quenna's warning becomes "before the weather turns on the hill road". Book 3 stands as written. The owner may later rule on the series calendar.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:73:- **O1 Season names.** The series calendar is season-blind in Book 5: weather words only, and no month order (#35, #36.4).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:74:- **O2 Cael's birthday.** It stays "the eleventh of Sowing" and is never set beside a season word. The owner may still choose "the third of Reaping" (#35).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:123:- **Season-blind B6 (#19 vs #35/#37 O1):** #19's restructure keeps its SHAPE (one academic year; served on the eighth day; the cache and Vastin before the midyear recess; the ruling in the year's last month; the Line crossed after the year's close) but carries NO season or month names — "the year's first weeks", "the cold term", "the midyear recess", "the year's last month", weather words for texture. "December" is struck. Owner may restore seasons when the series calendar is ruled (#35, #36.4).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:124:- **The birthday in B6:** a fixed date ("the eleventh of Sowing" default under #35; never beside a season word), with no cross-year day count and no month-of-year ordinal stated. The edition's own counts put the B5→B6 interval near 205 days, so the series calendar must later decide whether the academic year, the recess or the birthday moves. Owner item.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:140:- **The book's last line and the six restored units** (Gault's last note; the personnel query; the waystation board; "You couldn't read me…"; Cael's reply to Daeva; the closing exchange) are verbatim from the protected wording, with only the edition's mandatory changes ("Since my Kindling"; "Nine fragments"; the personnel query's teaching-assistant role, calendar and house frame).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:148:- **Season-blind and feet/yards, continued into Book 7** (as #37 O1 and #42 did for Books 5 and 6). Named seasons and metric units are replaced, minimally, INCLUDING inside Book 7's protected lines (for example "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." becomes "After the thaw. …"; "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." becomes the same distance in yards). Generic "season" and "month" stay. Every changed protected line is listed, old and new, in `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md`; the owner may restore any or all when the series calendar is ruled.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:149:- **Time since Kindling** (#18 extended to Book 7): the protected first pole "I've spent four years being the case the instruments couldn't parse" reads "Since my Kindling I've been the case…".
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:150:- **The birthday:** day 102 past the Line stands, never beside a season, a month order or a count back to the last birthday. By the edition's own day counts the two birthdays fall roughly 225 days apart (Book 6's mid-year, the year's close near day 207, then 102 days). The prose never states it; the series calendar remains the owner's to rule (#35, #42).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:154:## 49. Book 7 — protected Quiet-line / Kindling wording (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 4)
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:155:Seven protected lines say variants of "mine didn't", "my Path", "mine has been asleep since I was fourteen", "dark since fourteen", "every Path … his had not". Edition canon (Book 6): Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and the Arbiter went dark; he has no Path. At a Quiet line the others' live Arbiters stop, his is dark before and after, and his fragments still answer. **Default until ruled: the protected lines stay verbatim**, the surrounding plan and prose state the canon, and the lines read as Cael's own shorthand. Options: (1) release only the conflicting clauses for a minimal canon repair; (2) release the affected log entries for clean re-composition; (3) keep as is (the default).
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:157:**#49 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 4).** Read closely, most of the seven lines already agree with canon as written: the first says the others' ARBITERS stopped and "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen."; the fourth says "whatever I am isn't a Path"; Karis's struck line says "one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line". Only two use "Path … mine" loosely ("Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't"; "every Path in this camp stops, and mine doesn't"). Default confirmed: all seven stay verbatim as Cael's log shorthand; Movement 4's packet carries a binding note that narration and dialogue never say "his Path" and state the canon exactly (the five live Arbiters stop; his has been dark since Kindling; the fragments still answer). If the owner prefers, only those two clauses need releasing.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:165:The protected second pole closes Movement 6 (ch44, written at the well as day 111 breaks): "…We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." On this edition's calendar "tomorrow" is day 112, a road to Lowmarch's board; the next quiet ground entered is the Stair on day 114. The count is also arguable: the six have gone in at the Fallow once as a party (day 96), or twice if the first crossings at the line are counted. Sol's audit found no honest gloss. **Default until ruled: the line stays word for word, where the plan places it, unglossed.** Options: (1) keep as is (the default); (2) keep the words and move the entry to the night of day 113, the eve of the Stair, where "tomorrow" is true (Movement 6 would then close on Oryn's leaving); (3) supply replacement wording. Options 2 and 3 change published chapters.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:171:- **#53 (needed before Book 8 Movement 4).** Protected "it took four years and a hearing to walk out". The plan itself notes the figure does not fit the academy span; #18 bars numbers for time since Kindling, and Book 7's first pole was amended on that ground. **Default:** verbatim, as Cael's rough spoken figure, never repeated as fact. Options: (1) the default; (2) release only "four years" for wording without a number, as was done for Book 7's first pole; (3) settle the series calendar so that it is true.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:177:- **#56 (Book 8 Movement 2 or 3, Thornwater).** `"Five months and twenty days."` — Lira's arm, from the Ring to its release. It is true on the plan's day count (day 96 to day 265–266) but only if a month is thirty days, and #35 says the prose never states month lengths. **Default:** verbatim. Options: keep; "A hundred and seventy days."; or a wording without a figure.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:178:- **#57 (Book 8 Movements 8–9; extends #49).** Three protected lines speak of Cael's "Path" or say the machine never lit for him: `Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died.`; `His Path did not die. It also did not notice it should have.` (narration); `a machine that lit for everyone but him` (narration). Edition canon since Book 6: he has no Path; his own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, and it went dark. **Default:** verbatim; nothing else in the book says "his Path". The two narration lines are the hardest to square, since they are not Cael's own shorthand. Options: release the clauses for a minimal canon repair (Sol drafted wording, kept in the re-run report); or keep as is.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:180:Applied under standing decisions, and listed old and new in `B7-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md` so any can be restored: Book 8's named seasons (#48) and its three "five years" counts since Kindling (#18), the same changes Books 5–7 made.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md:191:The protected unit (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 5) reads "Deep layer. Sequence initiated" [a Compact date] "Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —". The source prints no value either ("She gave the date. It was a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it"). Sol's plan audit asked for an owner-supplied date. **Coordinator default:** the edition does as the source does — the sheet shows a date in the office's reckoning and the page never gives its figures, in Movement 2 or at the spring in Movement 3 (where Cael knows it for his Kindling day; no span of years is computed, #18). If the owner wants a printed registry date, it has to be minted and reconciled with #35/#42 (the series calendar), and ch12 and the spring scene re-touched.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:1:# Movement brief 006 — Before the Paths
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:12:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 2 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Vastin's second paper is "the page": a COPY in his own hand** of one line from an old register ("—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"). It was never cut from anything and is never called a leaf; "the leaf" is the chamber record of Movement 6 only. (2) **The technician's sheet carries a Compact date (a registry year and a day in it) that is NEVER printed as figures** anywhere in this book; whoever reads it reads a date, and the page does not give its numbers. The office filed that sheet at the end of the second row of the records, and it lies there. (3) **The anomaly column:** on every survey abstract, in every hand, for six years, the entry is the one word *Total* — an entry, not a sum. (4) **The Fallow completion report** carries five strokes for a name and a count of six (locked Book 7), not five written names. (5) **What Vastin has told the six about the layer is four things only:** no key (it cannot be reached); the citation; the suppressed records; the technician's line. He has not defined "classification event" and does not know which event is meant. Nothing on the page says that menders, technicians or any office have tried to open it or know more. (6) **Speakers:** "What follows you," was Lira's; "She's right. Go and lie down, and don't take the stairs fast," was Oryn's. (7) **Deployment since the Line is thirty** at the end of Movement 2 (the Iron read at the landing on the 277th). Purse 118 marks. (8) **Teague's spear** has "he/his" on the page from chapter 7 (OWNER-pending #59 as defaulted). (9) Vastin has shown no Iron Wall, has no stated age, has asked only for a bed, and holds Karis's unsealed receipt. Cael has not touched the page and has not read the sheet's date closely.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:14:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 3 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Deployment since the Line is thirty-two** at the end of Movement 3 (one Ember grain and one Wind burst away, both at the cut on the 279th). Ten fragments; the eleventh has not come; nothing came of standing two feet from Vastin's wall. Purse 138 marks. (2) **Iron Wall has been shown once** (the cut): a plane from a line struck with the stick, wall to wall, rooted — he may not lift a foot — loud to anything that hunts a Path, and it spent him to the floor. **Vastin's RIGHT knee** was bitten there; Oryn shut the holes and bound the joint with laths for a month from the 279th (stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall); he said "I cannot undertake" and has kept it to the letter. Brom's right foot, two toes, ten days from the 279th. (3) **The date:** Cael and Seln each know that the technician's sheet carries the day of Cael's Kindling. Neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. No figures are ever printed, no span of years is computed, and there is **no second calendar or offset** (one registry reckoning only). Vastin does no date arithmetic and knows nothing of it. (4) **The records at the spring:** Karis has matched FOUR sign-groups to the hide and has given NO number of places; no fifth place has been described. The same stroke and bar stands in a ruled square on all four matched places' sheets (in the field: stake thirty-two and the fourth site's thirty-fours only). The remark "Behaves as device. Cannot be." is on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; its hand is NOT identified. The instruments column reads true on every line. (5) **Seln has taught one thing, to Vastin** ("Draft nothing. Just look."). Cleon has been named (by Karis) and nothing more is known of him than her protected lines give. (6) **Oryn** went north from the fork on the 281st with the brown mule, her linen and her crossbow with one bolt; Millrace in three weeks; she owes Cael the reading ("the one thing I'm walking up that road owing"); the station term is written in the log. Her past as told at the fork: a house for the sick in a city inside the Line, the column for the patient's tier, a woman from the river sheds mended off the sheet; she has not been through a gate since. (7) **Loads:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; the tarred kit case on Vastin, taken up unasked at the fork-stone; Karis the flat and the hide, with the copied page in oilcloth in her coat. **Cael laid his hand on that page once, on the rise.** Vastin has walked beside Cael since the rise. (8) **Stillhounds:** a den that has learned a road runs to where a declaration ends (Karis's sixth line). The sixty yards of four-strand rope are still owed to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:16:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 4 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Who is where on the 284th:** inside the iron door are Cael, Brom, Lira, Vastin and Karis, with three boxes, the tarred kit case, the flat and the hide; Cleon let them in, counted loads and not people, and shut the door. The unnamed yard clerk is outside; **Seln is above ground, NOT on the card or the count**, watching who comes to the door. Oryn is two gates north with the brown mule. (2) **The count:** Karis is the card's unnamed bearer; Cael, Brom, Lira and Vastin are the four hands, entered by count; the clerk asked nothing and wrote *four*. None of the four restricted names has been written anywhere; the asset-restriction is still pending. Cards are good only for the day written on them and are torn at each gate; Iron passes the second wall and Bronze the third by right, on a certificate that is read out and written. The way to the registry's yard is the load lane under the third wall and a cut of **twenty-two steps in five flights, a stride and a half wide, walled three men high with no door or window**; it never crosses the square. Cael has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; Lira keeps the same discipline unasked. (3) **Cleon's terms** (given at the cook-house on the 283rd): all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is never said aloud by him); **nobody tells him what the sheets are or how old until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He has seen one drawn sheet and knows there are three places and fifty-two sheets, older than what the Compact found; he has not noticed Cael. **His Path has not been shown.** "Rune Path. Bronze." is all that is known of it, from Seln. (4) **Cael:** ten fragments; deployment thirty-two; the fourth and fifth self-readings were made on the 281st, round the still place and not in, uncounted; Tide feels only what flows and returned nothing ("a cord on a stone… *no length*"); he needs an instrument for what does not move, and owes Oryn the telling at the mill. Lira has read the log. (5) **Vastin and Cael:** Vastin has told him why he declined the second reading (the Ostrand case, causal; and a private relief at never learning what a plate would say); Cael has told him that the place was read twice and returned nothing, and nothing of what reads. Ground, not friendship. Vastin carries three sheets under one seal that he will not show; he has sat three times; his right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th (stick; no kneeling, running or wall) and he caught a slip on the steps with his left hand. Brom's two toes: five days left on the 284th. Lira's arm: day nineteen out of wool; her registry paper unshown; the ladder did not pull. (6) **The inn:** the long loft over the stable, by the yard half-door (the painted door has a book), for a week from the 282nd, pot at dusk, seven bowls; **purse 136 marks**. The outer gate counts feet on a bead-frame and writes no name. (7) **Stone:** the grey bridge, the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the iron door's frame are one dark dry-laid stone older than the walls; Karis has seen it and stated no conclusion beyond "the bridge was first". The iron door has no lock or handle outside; the clerk knocks. (8) The sixty yards of four-strand were priced at the rope-walk and are to be bought going out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:18:> **[Coordinator rulings after the Movement 5 audit, 2026-10-11 — binding; they override any plan text below that differs.]** (1) **Eleven fragments; deployment since the Line thirty-two; purse 134 marks** at the end of Movement 5 (the night of the 290th). The eleventh, Iron-Wall-adjacent, came from Vastin in the alley's quiet minute; it did not fill, it *set*; its prompt is *This far?*; it has not been deployed and **Vastin has not been told** (Cael holds that as a debt he cannot yet pay; Lira has read the log). (2) **How acquisition lines are printed in this book:** the protected "Fragment eleven" and "Fragment twelve" units are CAEL'S OWN cataloguing of what he reads — set once, in italics, framed as his plain words; they are NOT printed as a system block and take no FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading or code fence. (3) **The Deepstacks:** an iron door with a sliding bar inside; twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine; three galleries. Middle gallery about 110 strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at its end, a shelf above it with a jar, a tied bundle ("Paper. Not stone.") and the black oak plank's sacking; the fifty-two sheets on three tables, 11/29/12; the plank stands against the third table. Eastern gallery: the old town's tall tally-books. One CARRIED lamp, Cleon's, held "a hand to the left" (Cael holds it and has begun to put it where the eyes are about to go). The boxes go up at the clerk's bell and come down each morning on a fresh card; the clerk writes *The same* and *four*. (4) **Cleon** knows Karis's name (he heard Brom say it and has used it once); his own is on the card and has never been said aloud. He has shown his Path from OUTSIDE only (bear / carried / nothing; "They're orders."; "Same make."; the limit: it does not work on a river, a man or a tree, and costs his eyes for an hour). **His week runs from the 287th to the 293rd.** He has not noticed Cael and knows nothing of the alley or the mechanism. (5) **Karis** has fourteen of twenty-three letters and reads numbers and number-words only; seven kinds bear, twenty-three are carried, eleven are nothing; the bundle is tied and unread; Vastin's copied page is in her coat, unshown to Cleon. Her LEFT palm has seven stitches of Brom's under a strip of his shirt; she writes with the right. (6) **Vastin:** his right knee went again in the alley on the eleventh day of Oryn's thirty (a wall on it against her order, which he heard and asks that she be told); re-splinted with a slat from Brom's box, twice its size; on the night of the 290th he cannot stand or hold a bowl. He gave his name, rank and office aloud at the yard hatch on the 285th; nothing of it was written. He still knows nothing of what Cael carries. (7) **Brom:** the left (good) shoulder wrenched under a dray on the 286th and worse after the alley; he carries his box on the bound right shoulder, a debt entered for the mill's healers; the broker's offer (a guard's post inside the second wall) was answered "I'll think on it." and declined in fact. Lira: day twenty-five out of wool on the 290th; a bruised right shoulder; she drops from heights without the arm. (8) **Seln:** a registry clerk knows his face and voice (the price of a truthful answer at the hatch); he watches from the roof above the cut. His case is **SHUT** — never "unopened" (this edition's Book 6 opened it for the five) — and its contents are named nowhere in this book. He has seen one watcher three times (horseman's boots with the spur-rests cut away). (9) **The faction** (six, hooded, no faces, no Path opened) knows the loft and has shown that it knows; it saw Vastin's wall, a rock, a knife and a boy who stood still, and nothing of quiet ground or the fragments. Cael has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again. The loft is paid to the 295th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:22:> Packet 006 carries the 291st, borrowed handcart, Karis's bound left hand, eleven fragments, and the fact that three clerk questions remain unasked (`MOVEMENT-006.md:26–28`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving particulars:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:26:> - **Cleon's knowledge and statements.** Cleon knows Karis's name and has used it once; he knows the hand, has externally demonstrated bearer/carried/ornament and “orders,” has stated both limits, has matched the same make, and has delivered the documentation/built-twice close. His week runs from the 287th through the 293rd. He has not noticed Cael, learned of the alley, shown the inside/lean, or acquired knowledge of the mechanism (`chapter-27.md:187–199`; `chapter-29.md:193–289`; `chapter-30.md:253–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:117`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:31:> - **What the faction knows.** It knows the loft and has deliberately shown that knowledge. It saw Vastin's uncovered face and Iron Wall, plus a rock/knife/still boy, but no Path from another crew member, no face of its own was secured, and it saw nothing of quiet ground or Cael's fragments. Seln's finding is that it wanted a visible declaration and a carried box and avoided being entered itself (`chapter-33.md:247–289`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:32:> - **Inn, purse, count and day.** Six are in the long loft over the stable; it is paid through the 295th, with pot at dusk and seven bowls. Purse 134, reserve sealed in the third box. The below-ground daily count remains Karis as bearer plus four hands; Seln is never one of them. Night of day 290 is complete; Movement 6 opens day 291. The cut will not be climbed at dusk again, but no further route ruling has been made (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `chapter-33.md:277–305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:101–103,123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:33:> - **Lira and remaining objects.** Lira is day twenty-five out of wool, has a bruised right shoulder, and the left arm took nothing. Three boxes, kit case, flat and hide are in the loft; the 291st card is there; the shortened watchman's stave is with Seln; two plain bolts remain in the cut; sixty yards of four-strand are still owed and Brom means to buy them going out (`chapter-33.md:285–307`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:107,123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:46:It is the 291st day. After the alley the working party goes by the carts' street in daylight, with the boxes on a borrowed handcart. Karis's left hand is bound in a strip of Brom's shirt. Cael has eleven fragments and the eleventh has nothing to do. The clerk has not asked three things.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:50:This movement holds the book's reveal and the arc's second pole. The twelfth arrives at a word and carries a warning. A parcel brings the second half of a competence, and the largest instrument on the continent does a wrong thing once, for him. Then the leaf is read aloud **once**, and that night Cael takes it on his feet: not excluded but *prevented*, and he happened anyway. **This is a deliberately quiet movement, with one set piece.** The reason is that the reveal must land as a discovery on paper by a researcher, and the fire must hold. The physical pressure is the tail chase and the faction's presence in the streets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:53:- **The reader (291st).** Cleon shows the Path from inside: "A record sits … An instruction *leans* … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." Then **the acquisition at "there"**. The fifth row leans, and so does the board, and Cael does not turn the twelfth on anything else. He tells Lira first on the stair ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then goes back down and tells Cleon at the bell, in the order he has it. "You did what." "That's not in the classification system. That's not *supposed* to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water, and **the warning, verbatim**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael carry the case up the stair together. **The notice on the stair, verbatim**, with *He looked away. Kept.* The eyes are paid on the last flight. **"Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:54:- **Rune practice (~2,000, folded across the days).** The twelfth leans at every made thing: the inn table's joints, the bridge's arches, the dividers' hinge. He learns not to look, as he learned not to look at the light. It is never used on a person.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:55:- **The tail (291st–292nd night; ~2,500 set piece).** Seln and Cael follow a hood through the outer district. The hood goes through a tier gate Cael cannot legally cross, and he stops at the line. No faces, none taken, nothing learned but the faction's patience.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:56:- **Dividers (292nd).** The parcel and **Hesk's note, verbatim**. The meal: four marks, two cups kept, and Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"), leaving 130. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." This is **the first inventory written inside walls** (§12 C10). **The light, not steady for a count of one:** "an instrument turning toward him." It is the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross. The promise holds at its first cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:57:- **The leaf (293rd morning).** Describe the object before the reading: horn-coloured, point-written, the scraped name with its first upright stroke. Karis reads it **aloud once** (§9; §10 Tier A 1), then paraphrases it once: "the Architect" is a title, about four hundred years ago, and the purpose is the un-bound. "Older. Made. Us." Cael catalogues the room, not himself. **The chronicle** is marked: "Marked." / "Marked." Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers with **two pages** and the ruler rule. The copy, with the gap drawn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:58:- **The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. Cael gives **Lira the page to read first**; nobody explains it to her. "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom prices it. Seln will keep the cache "a while longer". Karis says two pages, then sleeps on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, taken on his feet and not catalogued, verbatim. "I want to stand in the middle of it." Cleon leaves: "Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:61:**Cutaways (~4,500):** Vastin, ~2,000, alone after the leaf. "Aimed." His sentence stays stopped in his head too. **He does not join the leaf to the sigils, does no date arithmetic, and names no seals.** Oryn, ~2,500, at a hold on her route, where a fourteen-year-old's Kindling happens. She watches a child see a sigil nobody else can see, and thinks of a dark one. **She has not heard the leaf. Nobody dies.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:66:- **The reveal is spoken once.** "Four hundred years" appears only in the record's voice, in Karis's single paraphrase, and in Cael's pole-two sentence. "The Architect" is a title, never an agent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:69:- The twelfth is not turned on Cael's own still place in this movement. It does not turn unbidden until Millrace (Movement 7).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:1:# BOOK MAP — The Fractured Path, Book 8: Before the Paths (Monroe Jackson 1.3 edition)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:13:**The title:** "Before the Paths" names two things. It is the era before the classification existed, when the un-bound walked in the land. It is also the book's argument: everything in Valdris was laid on top of a buried thing by someone who wanted it to stay buried. The book's image is a Compact registry built on the roof of a pre-Compact quarry it has never read.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:27:- **Teague's crew:** stays through the cold term at Lowmarch's upper inn: four practitioners plus the older healer of no Path, all unnamed except Teague. His exact term is: `After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes.` / `Noted.` He has the cold road; the five have the axe-head fence. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:29:- **Pike/the Compact:** Pike has nine completed lines under the five names; the ninth is the Stair and reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The first-snow season line is written with no number against it. The five names remain **eleventh**. The Compact has a Fallow completion report, the Stair rim's observations and a clerk's packet saying the crew kept the kit; it does not know that fragments work inside. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4] It has reached across the Line twice: on paper (the Fallow completion report) and in person (the six on the Stair's rim). The asset-restriction is pending. **Vastin is still inside**, writing nothing, with one window in Book 7. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:30:- **Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon. All six know the still-place phenomenon; only Cael and Oryn are shown hearing/saying its label. Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know the fourth-site survey; Oryn, Teague and Pike do not know that result at entry. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:34:- **Cael:** nineteen, with **thirteen confirmed fragments**. Iron Wall came from Vastin in the Treswick alley (entered, **not told**; the debt stands; deployment none). Rune came from Cleon in the chamber (told to Cleon; the warning stands). Force came from Teague at the Span's barricade (first and only use on stone at the pass; the recoil stops in the ribs; never used on a person). **The still place** has been read by two instruments and understood by neither. Tide reads nothing, with everything going round it. Rune reads a shape with bones, a floor with nothing built on it. At the court's centre there was **no edge**: "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made." **He told no one the Rune finding.** His Arbiter is dark and unchanged. The instruments read wrong in his hands and only his, with the **trend up** (a hair at Lowmarch; a stride short and "a hair and a half, two" at the plain's edge). That fact is unsourced. 123 marks; nothing owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:35:- **The reveal is delivered once, in the record's voice:** the leaf in the Deepstacks. "The Architect" is the record's title; the name is scraped away; it was about four hundred years ago; the purpose was "that the un-bound should not come again". The chronicle's "went into the ordering he had made, and is in it —" is **marked, not read**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Vastin** is on the stick until the thirtieth day of Oryn's treatment month [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] ("Thirty's the month"). He walks with the five **unadmitted**. He has not asked to join and nobody has asked him.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:41:- **Teague** turns west with three practitioners and the healer of no Path. **The young one is dead**, buried under stone at the pass's east mouth. His name was said once by the broad man and is never written. [OWNER-pending #54] Teague carries Cael's letter to Hesk. "After the next thaw. Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:53:1. **KEEP — The cold-term frame (S1, 131st–264th).** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] The ferry has gone and the count has stopped moving. Inventory: nineteen, ten fragments, 96 marks. The cold stay is priced [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]: "Meadow rate is four a month for a crew that's on my sheet" / "Eleventh", twenty paid in front, leaving 76. Teague's chin-lift across the yard; the season line left blank on purpose.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:58:6. **KEEP — Thornwater (265th–266th).** The ford in thaw. Oryn's yard. Lira's arm is released ("Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off."). Lira asks, for the first time since Norhold: "Will you mend it." / "Lie still". The ankle is mended. "Thank you." / "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks." The map on Thornwater's table: "That's a line." Cael tells her about the cord: "I don't know what that is. Neither do you. Write that down too." Oryn comes down because Lowmarch and Millrace are her first stops after the thaw [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. Nobody asked her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:60:8. **KEEP — The ferry (277th).** Vastin arrives alone, in a brown coat, with an ash stick, a pack mended with cord and a bad knee. "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." Pike prices him: "What'd he do?" → "Then he's nothing yet." He pays a copper and a half for bread. Teague reads his hands a step longer than a crew looks. Lira's face for men in grey doesn't fit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:62:10. **KEEP — The handover (277th evening)**, in Vastin's stated order. First, the records: a courier's flat of six years of survey abstracts, the anomaly column ("Total"), six rows, "More than four", and the completion report as the last sheet. Second, the page: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". Third, the technician's sheet: the deep-layer line and the brush bar; Karis copies it and writes "not read". Seln goes still and does not say the sum. Vastin's vertigo; Karis owns the response. Cael's hand stays a hand's width from the page. Nobody says *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:64:12. **KEEP — The cut (279th).** Iron Wall is first shown: a plane across the road, rooted, and therefore loud. Brom fights silent with a rock. Lira works the scree. Cael bursts away, then goes still on the scree; the pack turns back and breaks on the wall. The heap. Seln in the heap. Five dead and three into the sink. Costs: Brom's foot; **Vastin's knee**, bound by Oryn for "a month". The lesson: "The wall held the line. And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." / "You do now." The log (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:65:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (the date matches his Kindling day; "six years" is the office's survey-record rounding; no numeric span since Kindling is computed [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 7]), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:73:21. **KEEP — The marks (285th–287th).** The lamp trade. Cleon's board is matched to the Hall's fourth sheet: bearer, carried, ornament. "They're orders." **The limit**, verbatim. "Same make." Cael wants it turned on himself and does not say so. **Brom's yard:** he rights a cart with his back, no Path, is offered the life, and picks up the box on the bound shoulder. "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." **Seln's night walk** from a roof below the walls: "I looked at it." Vastin: "How long did it take you." / "I was fourteen. I'm nineteen. I'm not there yet either." Cleon's close (§10). The 288th–289th are undramatized in the source.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:75:23. **KEEP — The reader (291st).** By the carts' street in daylight. Cleon's inside: "An instruction leans … This is a stair." Karis: "The strata lean too." **Acquisition at "there".** Cael tells Lira first ("Twelfth. His. Lean."), then Cleon at the bell. "You did what." "That's not supposed to be possible. That's —" / "No. I'll not say that one." The cup of water; **the warning**. "He went back to the carving." Vastin and Cael take the case up together. The notice on the stair. The eyes are paid on the last flight. "Cael did not tell anyone. He remembered."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:76:24. **KEEP — Dividers (292nd).** Hesk's parcel and note. The meal: four marks, two cups kept for Karis and Oryn, Seln's slip read and burned ("Closed"); 130 marks. Vastin and the cups: "Out here you count who's owed a seat." The first inventory written inside walls (§12 C10). **The station's light is "not steady" for a count of one**: a pressure, "an instrument turning toward him". It becomes the fourth entry on the page. He does not cross; the promise holds at its first cost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:77:25. **KEEP — The leaf (293rd morning).** It is read aloud **once** by Karis (§9). The chronicle leaf is **marked**. Vastin reaches ("the mark that is given at the kindling —") and Karis answers: two pages. The copy with the gap drawn. "Older. Made. Us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:78:26. **KEEP — The yard fire (293rd evening).** Seln is told on the street ("Made." "For a kind."). Cleon comes up, the only time. **Lira first:** "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Brom's price. Seln keeps the cache "a while longer". Karis's two pages, then she falls asleep on a bucket. Brom to Cleon: "Good." Vastin: imperfect → corrupt → "aimed … At a category. Which turned out to be a person. Who's sitting across the fire." Lira: "You signed the mark at kindlings." / "I would have." **Pole two**, said aloud (§10). "I want to stand in the middle of it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:80:28. **KEEP — The road east (295th–297th).** The bridge (five piers counted; the crown not looked at). The spring. The fork passed. The shoulder hold's factor: "He said you'd say that." **The cut revisited** ("Here"): the stick briefly off the ground; "Two words. Both of them ours." / "Noted." The feeling of being *known* is entered. Lowmarch at dusk on the 297th. Pike: "Treswick. Survey read. Bearing." The season line is dated. Cael no longer reads pages the other way round. **Teague's term and contract:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's; "Contract. Not more than that."; "The wall's still the wall."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:87:35. **KEEP — The shale camp (305th).** The blanket. The rows lean along the bearing. The point is fixed. **The lamps finding** (§10). Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Cael does not add his own third page (the Kindling date). **The directive and the objection**: "That's not a monolith. That's a crack." Seals unnamed. "The Compact … Yes. Part of it." The broad man's "Aye". The healers' third exchange (hands in the other's work). Seln on the pass. The fixed close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:91:39. **KEEP — The centre (307th dusk).** 506 strides. Rune turned on the floor at a hundred strides gives the same reading. The eyes are paid. **No edge, no seam.** "Not the Quiet." "Not a fragment." "The same kind of made." He fit. It was not an accident. The third sentence goes unsaid. Oryn reads him at the line ("May I?"): "The same finding." Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road. If there's road." He told nobody. The count. "Twenty-nine tomorrow." / "Thirty's the month."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:108:| **NEW — The shale-back herd at the axe-head fence** (cold weather) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | summarized as "we walked the fence" | 3,000 | A cold-weather set piece [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] needing no Path: a herd of armoured grazers sheltering on the fence line's slope must be moved without stampeding them ("lethal on a slope when herded wrong"). It teaches the Iron read on frozen ground, Lira benched by her sling, Seln's posts, and Brom reading a line. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:110:| **NEW — The silent yard** (cold-weather learning bouts with Teague's crew) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | absent | 3 bouts × ~1,500 = 4,500 | No Paths, steel and bodies only, in the frozen meadow. Cael loses to the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59]'s spear reach (she never speaks), then corrects. One-armed Lira coaches from the bench. The rival clock appears on the page. This must not touch the sequence locks in §13 (no wall drill; Seln teaches nobody). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:112:| **NEW — The ferry's first landing** (277th, high water) | quiet landing | 1,500 | Rope and flood. Vastin is seen holding a physical line, with no Path, before anyone knows it is him. Iron Wall must not show before the cut. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:113:| **NEW — The tail in Treswick** (291st–292nd) | absent | 2,500 | After the alley, Seln and Cael tail a hood through the outer district at night. The hood passes through a tier gate Cael cannot legally cross. The faction stays faceless and unlocated, and the promise and the bar become physical. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:123:5. **Rune practice and cost** (≈3,000). After the 291st Cael catches himself reading made things everywhere: the inn table's joints, the bridge's arches, the dividers' hinge. He learns that the eyes pay, and pays it in the dark (Millrace). It is never used on a person. He does not turn it on himself until it turns unbidden.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:129:- **The cold months (131st–264th)** [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] (≈14,000). The first week of ice. The pricing scene at the inn. The cold-term board [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6]. The fence trip. The river becoming a road. Hesk and Vell's letters gone west on the last ferry, with the answers pending. Karis's back room. The long dark. The thaw. Pike in his room. The source's log entries become scenes, and the log stays as punctuation between them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:144:| **Karis** | To be right and believed, with a primary source | Learns the kit. Makes the case for west. Owns the response to Vastin's flat. Reads the leaf once and asks that nobody say it back. Keeps two pages at a spring, a hole and a fire. Sits with Vastin after the pass. | 14 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:148:| **Cleon** | The work finished and believed, without leaving the Deepstacks | Sets terms at noon. Shows the inside of the Path to no one before Karis. Refuses to finish the sentence. Looks away from the boy deliberately. Comes up the stair once. | 6 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:150:| **Pike** | An honest ledger | Prices the cold term. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] Prices Vastin at nothing yet. Leaves the season line blank, then dates it. | 4 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:157:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:174:| 6 | Before the Paths | 34–40 | 34,000 | S13, S14, S15, S16 | The twelfth and the warning; dividers and the light's wrong count; the leaf read once; pole two at the fire. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:179:**Totals:** 60 chapters, 300,000 words. The first third (≈100,000) ends inside Movement 4 (around chapter 20). The middle third ends at the close of Movement 6 (chapter 40, ≈197,000).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **Vastin** | ≈8,000 (4) | M2: the last miles to the Line and the ferry (the three people who told him "go to the plank"; the page in his coat). M4: the outer district's "first honest district". M6: alone after the leaf ("aimed"). M9: the court's rim at night. | His career; what he read; the citation; "no key"; the technician's line **and the bar**; the completion report; his knee; his own declining of the second reading. | **The date's arithmetic.** He never computes the deep-layer date against Cael's Kindling. The integration mechanism (he is never told). The directive and the objection before the 305th. The two seals' names. Any wish to *ask* to join, or any vote (Book 9). The Arbiter–apparatus connection (his sentence stays stopped even in his head). |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:194:| **Karis** | ≈7,500 (3) | M1: a cold night [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] with the kit's index (her want; the cord reads wrong only for him, and she refuses a theory). M5: decipherment (board numerals; the first letters). M8: the night after the lamps finding (the refusal held in her own head). | The sheets; strata; the index (as unreadable until the 298th); the leaf (after the 293rd); the lamps finding. | The Rune finding (nobody knows it). The integration of Rune before Cael tells Lira. **Drawing the line**: her interior names that the sentence exists and refuses it. The deep-layer date as Cael's Kindling. The leaf's content before it is read aloud. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:195:| **Seln** | ≈7,500 (4) | M3: the spring, doing the sum and setting the sheet. M5: the night walk on the roof with the cache. M8: the crest at night or the perimeter before the Span. M9: the ridge with Lira to recover the mule. | The sum (the date ≈ Cael's Kindling day), unspoken; the office's habits; the faction's craft; the cache's existence and weight. | **The cache's contents** (it stays unopened). Any decision about the cache. Any theory of what the deep layer is. The Rune finding. Teaching anyone before Vastin at the spring. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:196:| **Oryn** | ≈7,000 (3) | M4: the north circuit (Oxhollow's gate; the wrist; a birth). M6: a hold child's Kindling witnessed from outside. M9: the night after the first death. | Her readings; the still place as "nothing, everything round it"; twelve then thirteen currents; the mechanism (her Tide was taken at her direction). | **The leaf** (she has not heard it). The Rune finding. Any patient dying under her hands before the pass. An explanation of "Same as you". No cutaway at the court itself. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:220:| 279 | The cut; **Vastin's knee (Oryn's month: day 1 = 280)**; 138 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:260:| **Iron Wall (Vastin's Path)** | Witnessed at the cut (M3) and the alley (M5) | Rooted; the man is the plane's foot; it cannot chase; it is loud to anything that hunts discharge; reserve spent to the floor; the knee | Shown three ways: road (punished), corridor (rewarded), slant (the pass) |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:262:| **Rune Path (Cleon's)** | Taught from outside in M5 (bones), from inside in M6 (lean) | Structure, not meaning; made things only; not a river, not a man; eyes for an hour; no use in a fight | — |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:264:| **Force Path (Teague's)** | Seen in the meadow (M7) and at the barricade (M8) | Line of the frame at contact; needs a thing to push against; a body's length; recoil back along the line (wrist, then elbow; a splint warning) | — |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:268:| **The Arbiter** | Checked M9 | Dark since Kindling; nothing for the Quiet to take | Unchanged |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:279:- Tiers and Paths in Teague's crew, in Vastin, and in Treswick's machinery (Copper/Iron/Bronze/Silver; passes; tier gates; the smith's two forges; the provision's columns).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:323:- **The cut (M3).** A hundred strides of road cut to a cart's width, with scree on both sides and a frozen runnel a stride wide down the middle. A sink lies fifty-five yards below [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] on the north side, iced and in shadow; there are eight hounds. Positions: Brom on stone at the south edge with a rock; Vastin a stride behind him; Lira on the south scree; Seln on the north scree, unseen; Cael twenty strides west, past the sink; Karis, Oryn and the mule at the east end. The decisions: the wall goes up and everything turns to the loudest thing; Brom and Lira work its south end silently; Cael bursts **away**, then goes still on the scree as the lock beat lands; the pack returns to the wall and breaks on it; the heap; the runnel. The opponent learns too: the den has learned the road. Costs to carry: Brom's foot; Vastin's knee (a month); Cael's burst bill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:327:- **New set pieces** (shale-back fence; ice road; silent yard; Lira's bout; ferry landing; the tail; the seep). Each develops a problem the reader can follow: terrain, positions, objective, limit, a change of decision, and a cost carried forward. **Never put a Path or declaration on display that a sequence lock forbids** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:333:- **The leaf is read aloud once**, by Karis, in the chamber, on the 293rd morning (M6). It is not quoted again by anyone who heard it. Cael gives Lira the page to read; nobody says it back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:335:- **"The Architect"** is the record's **title** ("a title, not a name; the name's gone"). After the leaf it appears again only as a historical comparison ("as old as the Architect"). Nobody uses it as a present agent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:337:- **The un-bound / [UNBOUND]:** the word is live as a historical *kind* in the leaf. Before that, Karis uses it once as a stratum limit ("Older than [UNBOUND]") at Cleon's table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:338:- **Two pages, no line.** The leaf and the lamps finding are never joined: not in dialogue, not in any interior (including cutaways), not in the narration. Vastin's sentence stops twice (in the chamber; on the shale). The words *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* are never used for Arbiters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:349:1. **The leaf (S15):** "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:351:3. **Karis's copy and finding (S15):** "and the" [gap drawn] "set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it." / *Older. Made. Us.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:352:4. **Vastin's page (S3):** "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:360:12. **Fragment eleven (S12):** "Iron-Wall-adjacent. Vastin. Partial. Iron family. Held. A plane, not a body: the ground told not to give. Distinct from the third — Iron-adjacent, the bed; this is not the bed hardened, this is a line drawn on it and kept. Engagement field: defensive; rooted. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:361:13. **Fragment twelve (S13):** "Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth." Then: *He looked away. Kept.* *Not a man.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:366:17. **Pole two (S16):** Lira: "So the whole time they weren't afraid you'd break something. They were afraid you'd *exist*." Cael: "Since my Kindling I thought the system forgot to make room for me," … "It didn't forget. It was *built* so there'd be no room. Four hundred years of a whole world, so that I wouldn't happen." … "I happened anyway." / Lira: "Yeah." … "Now what." / Cael: "Now we find out how old the oldest one is. Karis has a bearing and the marks, and the records to read them against. There's a site at the end of the line that's been quiet since they built the machine." … "I want to stand in the middle of it." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:371:22. **Departures (S24):** Teague: "The thaw's past," / "Noted," / "After the next thaw." … "Whatever's on the next line. My crew comes." / Oryn: "The day I have to." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that." … "They'll carry. They'll hurt," … "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say." / Seln: "Six. Six and no mule. Nothing behind. Nothing beside." / "West," Cael said. / "West," said Brom, and picked up the box. / "Twenty-nine tomorrow," / "Thirty's the month," [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:374:25. **Oryn at Millrace (S18):** "There's a place in you I can't read because it isn't *flow*. I've spent my life reading flow. Whatever that is, it's not the kind of thing my Path was built for." / "Then it's not mine." … "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." … "Lie still when I say. That's still the term." / "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:375:26. **The rate (S19 log):** "Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:391:- **Ch1 closing log (270th):** "The ferry runs when the ice goes. Karis has a bearing, an index she can't read, and a language she can't read, and she says the answers are in a border archive nobody's opened since before the Compact. Since my Kindling I've stayed out of registries because a registry is where they file you. She wants me to walk into the oldest one on the continent. The kit reads everyone but me. So does the world, mostly. Nineteen. Ice goes next week. West, and inside, for the first time since the academy above Ostrand — which is a sentence I did not think I'd write again." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] And the 168th: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:392:- **Thornwater:** "Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off." / "Will you mend it." / "Lie still" / "It's an arm. Use it. It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year and then it won't. Don't fall on it." / "I don't know what that is." … "Neither do you. Write that down too."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:393:- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:395:- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of." [OWNER-pending #52]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:402:- **S12:** "I put the wall in front of it anyway. I'd like that entered somewhere, since I'm not the one who keeps the ledger any more." / "It's entered," Log: "Eleventh. Iron Wall, from Vastin, in an alley, while he held a line for us with nothing behind him but the decision to. It's not Brom's — Brom gets harder, this holds. Since my Kindling I've learned to give ground and disappear. Now I've got the opposite in me, from the man who spent forty years being the wall they put in front of people like me. He held it for us instead. I don't have a word for what that is. I wrote it down anyway." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:405:- **S17 log:** "Karis cracked the grade. The sites are ranked by age and the bearing runs oldest-last — somebody laid them out in order, and the order runs into the deep edge, toward the first one they ever made. Second-tier's the fourth site, the one the Compact fenced. Third-tier's out past it, on the line, quiet for centuries. Teague's crew came after the thaw like he said — ten of us now, and he's still better at this than I am, and the ledger still says so. Two crews, one bearing, and a straightedge my guardian sent me because my grandmother said a man who catalogues everything eventually needs to draw a line through it. Turns out she was right about the line. Turns out the line was already drawn four hundred years ago. We're just the first to follow it to the end." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Also: "Two words," … "Both of them ours." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:406:- **S19:** "Nobody declares. Nobody dies. They're seven people on a posting. Noted?" / "Noted," / "You'll die in there." / "We've been in three times," / win sentence: "The crews had removed the watch's ability to hold the approach by making the only safe retreat a line the watch would not cross and the crews would." / Teague's arm: "A third time on that arm and I'll set it in a splint. That's not a healer's opinion. That's a fact about a line." / "Noted," / "Everybody says that now," Log body: "Twelfth—no, count it again—thirteenth. Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. Thirteen things that aren't a Path, and I got three of them in one city and one bridge. Rate's climbing and I'm writing that down because Hesk taught me to note the trend. The Span's the fourth site and the Compact fenced it, years ago by the scale on the iron, and left men on it. They knew. They've always known. The bearing runs through it and keeps going, oldest-last, and the oldest one's out there in the deep edge, quiet since they built the machine. One more site. I've wanted to stand in the middle of it since Karis said *someone made this.* Tomorrow I find out what standing in the middle of the first one feels like."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:407:- **S20 close:** "It's here," Karis said. "Third-tier, documented four hundred years back — as old as the record, as old as the Architect, as old as the machine. The first one they made, or near it." / "And it's on the line." / "It's the *end* of the line. Oldest-last. Everything before it was practice, or maintenance, or — I don't have the word. This is the one that's been quiet since before quiet had a name." … "You still want to stand in the middle of it." / "More than I've wanted anything since I was fourteen." / "Why." / "Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died. I want to know what the *oldest* one does to me. I think it's going to tell me something the records can't." [OWNER-pending #57] / He was right. He did not yet know how right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:410:- **S23 close:** "Every other one, yours worked and ours died." / "Yes." / "You think this one's different." / "I think this one's the first one they made," … "I think if any place on the continent is going to tell me what I am, it's the one they built to make sure I'd never be." / He stepped over the line. / His Path did not die. It also did not *notice* it should have. [OWNER-pending #57] / "Wait here," he said, and did not look back, and walked toward the center of the oldest quiet, alone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:411:- **S24 ledger:** "Thirteen: Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. One anomaly, the still place, read by two instruments — the tenth, which says nothing, and the twelfth, which says a shape — and understood by neither. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made. That is as far as the instruments go and I am not going past them." / "Stood in the middle of the first one. Nothing. Entered." **The letter:** "Nineteen. Your grandmother's line was already drawn. I followed it to the end; both edges agreed. Tell Lira's family I said so. Mind the shape, you said. I'm minding it. — C." [OWNER-pending #55] (§12 C11.) Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road," … "If there's road."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:412:- **Closing prose (S24):** "He had spent the whole year learning that the world was built to prevent him — four hundred years of tiers and registries and a machine that lit for everyone but him, all of it laid down so that what he was would never come again. And at the center of the first place they ever made, the oldest silence on the continent, the one built before there was a word for it, he had felt no exclusion and no prevention and no wall. He had felt at home. He did not have a word for that yet. But he knew, now, walking back out across a floor older than the system that had expelled him, that it was not an accident — that the place built to end him was the one place he fit — and that the difference between *the system was built to exclude me* and *the system was built to prevent me* had a third sentence past it, waiting, that he was not ready to write. Someone had made the pattern. He was, he was beginning to understand, the pattern. That was as far as he could say." [OWNER-pending #57] [OWNER-pending #58]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:420:| **The Fractured Path predates the classification system** (the Architect designed it; ~400 years; the purpose was the un-bound) | **8 — DELIVER** | Deliver once, in the leaf (M6), in the record's voice. Karis paraphrases it once. Name scraped; "the Architect" is a title. The narrative reports the record's rationale and **does not endorse it**. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:421:| The Arbiter system is the Architect's live infrastructure | 9 | Plants only: "Behaves as device. Cannot be."; "no key"; the lamps finding on its own page; the dark Arbiter unchanged. Never join the leaf to the sigils. No *terminal / circuit / infrastructure*. The Arbiter never speaks. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:422:| Cael is a recurrence (the tomb; the un-bound practitioner's record) | 9 | Never say "recurrence". No tomb, no hint of one. "The same kind of made" and "the pattern" are the ceiling. The third sentence stays unwritten. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:426:| The Architect's will is active and hunting Cael | 11 | Three deniable plant families only: (1) the running sub-layer sequence (S3/S5); (2) "is in it —", marked (S15); (3) the instruments and the station clustering on Cael, trending up (S1/S5/S14/S22, plus the Span row). Attributed in-world to his unreadability. "Made things do not know." Nothing says or implies agency. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:428:| The Fractured Path is primordial | 13 | Never *primordial / before / source* about Cael. Interior read as *structure*, felt not explained. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:429:| The Architect's motive was legitimate | 13–14 | The record's fear is reported, not sympathized with. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:439:- **C2 — Academy-era spans given as numbers.** Examples: "The Compact spent four years trying to file this boy" (S2); "I read your file for four years" (S7); the cache carried "four years" (S11, S16); "in the four years Cael had known him" (S5); "it took four years and a hearing" (S8, a fixed line). These sit against the locked timeline (Kindling at fourteen, academy from about sixteen) and OWNER-DECISIONS #9/#18 ("since his Kindling", no number, for B4–B6). **Edition:** no numeric span since Kindling. Anchor academy/cache spans to events; office survey records may keep their own six-year rounding where explicitly identified as the office's. The protected S8 four-year line remains word for word under [OWNER-pending #53] and is never repeated as fact. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:442:- **C5 — Rune's tier.** The universe bible says "Cael's twelfth (Rune-adjacent, partial, Bronze)". The notice says "Rune family … Tier equivalent unknown". **Edition follows the notice.** Bronze is Cleon's tier.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:443:- **C6 — Architecture residue.** The architecture's header, plant ledger and checkpoint still say Cael turns twenty in Ch14, the terminus is "the Still Court", and there is a "sixth" site. **Superseded** by rulings 12 and 13 and by the closed prose: nineteen throughout, "the court", the fifth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:447:- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:449:- **C12 — Office "six years" and the Kindling date.** "Six years" is the office's survey-record rounding. It is not paired with a numeric count since Cael's Kindling. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 11]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:476:- **The clerk** stays unnamed and "do not name" holds. He has not asked three things by the 291st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:482:**Names pending owner approval: none required.** Every new figure the expansion needs is carried by role: the axe-head hold's factor, the carter at the ice road, the ferryman and his boy, Oryn's route patients (at Oxhollow and unnamed holds), the hold child at the Kindling, the broker's men, and the hood in the tail. This keeps the audio load low in a book whose cast is already heavy with role-names (Teague's crew must stay unnamed by canon). If the author finds a recurring role that needs a name in the audio, it is listed here for approval before drafting, and drafted under the proposed name per the edition's policy (RUN-LEDGER 18:41).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:490:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three future holds and "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."; Teague's "After the next thaw" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael remains nineteen at the Book 9 opening. Do not place or calculate his next birthday until the owner rules the series calendar. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:1:# STATE LEDGER — Book 8: Before the Paths (Monroe 1.3 edition)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Nineteen; no birthday this book. Ribs quiet since day 129. His Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark. He has no Path. Ten fragments at rest; the still place untouched since Oryn's order. **Birthday rule:** never place either birthday beside a season name, month order or count back (OWNER-pending #42/#48). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:15:| Brom | Iron Skin; Copper formal. Right shoulder mended twice and not a third time this season; held in four yards of webbing by the drover's turn. Older healer: `It'll do.` [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:19:| Teague's crew | Staying through the cold term at Lowmarch's upper inn: Teague, tall spear man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59], broad crossbow man, young one, older healer of no Path. All but Teague unnamed. [OWNER-pending #54] [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 13] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:26:**Cael knows:** ten fragments with current costs/deployment notes; deployment since the Line is 27. The still place is a location under the breastbone, read three times, with all ten going round it and none through; `Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.` He has obeyed the no-touch order. Four sites lie on one map edge: Ring, Stair and Hall entered; fourth unentered, unnamed, undated and untested at 440 yards and two strides radius behind stake 34 repeated one per pace. The three entered sites stop live Arbiters while his already-dark Arbiter remains dark and his fragments answer. He has no Path; nobody knows why. He knows the kit's radius line, 41-kind index, stroke/bar and `third site confirmed on bearing`; Karis's `Someone made this pattern.` remains unanswered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:28:**Who knows the integration mechanism:** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Oryn — six. Oryn knows sources by Path and not by person except those she has touched; she does not know Seln supplied Shadow-adjacent. **Not** Vastin, Teague, Pike or Cleon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:40:**Oryn knows:** the mechanism by Path, the full still-place telling and label, and the three entered sites on one bearing. She left at the day-122 fork and does not know the day-123 fourth-site survey or result at entry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:44:**Pike knows:** the nine board outcomes, the first-snow season line and the crew's return record. He knows neither the mechanism nor what works inside.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:48:**He does not know:** that the index is a grade; the Architect; Treswick's archive or Cleon; anything Vastin carries; that instruments will read wrong in his hands. The last is discovered on the 168th (Book 7 ends with the instruments reading TRUE in his hand; Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:57:- **Pike:** nine completed lines under the five names. Ninth/Stair: *three hundred; taken; not paid*. First-snow season line written, with no number against it. Five names eleventh; Teague ten up. Fallow hundred and Stair 300 remain in Pike's box unmarked; neither is a crew-payable debt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:97:| Hesk, Vell | Letters. Hesk's next parcel (the dividers) arrives in Treswick on the 292nd. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:103:- "Someone made this pattern": answered in part by the leaf (Movement 6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:127:- **Thornwater, days 265–266:** Lira's arm released (OWNER-pending #56 "Five months and twenty days.", said by Lira); **Lira asks and Oryn mends the ankle** ("Lie still," Oryn said; "Thank you." said by Lira; "Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks."). Before this Lira had asked once, on the mountain in Book 7, and nobody since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:138:- **What four a month buys (flag):** the hearth's end; the pot at dusk, a bowl a head; and the crew's names said to anybody who comes asking. Not bread, candles, the back room or the mule. "A cold term's five by my book": twenty, in front. The keeper comes out to his own door, behind the plank, to hear his floor priced (the join for the restored `The keeper said, "Pike," and Pike said, "Eleventh."`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:143:- **The silent yard (flag):** a square trodden under the ash, twelve strides on a side, a hazel peg at each corner, a bench from the upper inn on its western edge. Teague's rules: three touches; "a touch is what the one who took it calls"; over the pegs is a touch; nobody strikes what a healer has had her hands on this season. The name is the three grey men's. Bouts on the 148th (three to none) and the 158th (three to one); a sack game on the 190th, three a side.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:145:- **Teague's wrist (flag):** the leather has been on it "since before the boy could lift a pack"; the joint is thicker than its fellow by the width of a finger; it "clicks"; "A Force paid where the line came out of him." The older healer binds it to her board at night and tells him to leave his Path shut till the thaw. A block lies on the second ledge of the cold road, with a herd lying up above it; he will shift it "as a carter would". The young one has brought him a hot cloth for it on every cold night since he joined. In his own window Teague is named as a Force for the first time in this edition. No Force is used on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:160:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventieth day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 131, 133, 138–146 (the fence; the herd on the 140th), 147, 148, 150, 158, 161, 168, 170 (Karis), 176, 190, 224, 230, 263, 264–265 (the saddle; the ford), 265–266 (Thornwater), 267–268 (down), 268, 270. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page. The river: shelf ice on the 131st; a road from the 154th; open at the middle on the 230th; "a week" from carrying a boat on the 268th; the scow's blocks being knocked out on the night of the 270th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:166:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. Her long knife has an edge again (the 181st). **Left arm released on the 266th: she undid Oryn's knot herself.** All eight marks pale. "It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year… Don't fall on it." It has held a boot and lifted a bench. **Right ankle mended on the 266th**, an hour on Oryn's plank; she stands on the ball of the foot. She wears the carter's great boot without its packing. She still has Oryn's crossbow and its one bolt (not mentioned as returned). She coached Cael's feet from the bench ("out" and "home") and the young one's. **She asked for the ankle on the 266th, and said "Thank you." to Oryn afterward; before that she asked nobody for anything in this movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:176:**Teague and his crew.** He proposed and ran the silent yard to make his people better at fighting with no Path. He sent the young one to learn from Lira. His wrist is bound shut till the thaw on the older healer's order. His term stands. He knows nothing of the mechanism; he has seen a light in the shed and a guard at its door, heard a Wind's crack on two nights, and watched a pair of boots refuse something three times. The tall one, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the five. Nobody in his crew is named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:178:**Pike's book and the cloth.** At the pricing the keeper said, "Pike," and Pike said, "Eleventh." **Eleven lines:** the tenth is the fence (*forty; paid*), the eleventh the rope-house roof. The season line's number is still blank, "on purpose". **Eleventh on the cloth**, unmoved all cold term. The ice road was "said, not entered".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:196:- **Lira:** her right ankle is newly mended; she walks on the ball of it and wears the oversized carter boot without its old stuffing. Her left arm is released but slow for a month, aches in wet for a year, and is not to be fallen on (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127-151`). She still has Oryn's crossbow, hook, and one bolt; no return occurs (`manuscript/chapter-02.md:7`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:283`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:205:**Movement 1 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Sol recheck of repair r1: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all four tracked passages RESOLVED against the source; no new tracking; every binding ruling above borne out by the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch3, the author's own "his Path" (of Teague) now reads "the Force"; ch6, Seln's sentence after Karis's protected speech now gives the asset-restriction as locked Book 6 ch58 states it — **the paper executes when an enrolled name is written in a book inside a district, and must be served within the hour** (not "a certificate inside the Line"). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report after the fixes. Final: 30,941 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (9 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment twenty-nine; day 270 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:215:- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:235:- **The new cloth (flag):** Pike paints a new cloth at the thaw; each crew's season figure is carried over and the cloth hangs in the order of the figures; "A hold reads down from the top until it comes to a crew that it can pay." The five have no figure, "So I carry the place": eleventh on the new cloth. Teague is first.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:239:- **Vastin as he arrives (flag):** a drover's coat of brown frieze, too short in the sleeve, bought "at the last market inside the Line"; the grey one left on its hook; an ash stick cut out of a hedge; a pack with one strap mended in cord; a small purse on a cord; the flat carried under the pack against his back, and **a single copied page** inside his coat in oilcloth. **The knee** "had begun to complain at about the hundredth mile and had left off being civil at the two hundredth"; no side is given; ten miles a day. He left "the seal of his office in the tray marked *done*, some months ago, on a morning of rain, with nothing written to go beside it". At the last station he looks in at the plate and remembers only what Book 5 shows: a plate, a file and a set of questions carried up a bluff, "and all three had told him nothing"; and that he declined a second reading and never said why. He crossed the sill on the 265th and reached the western landing on the evening of the 276th. His left hand would not open after the strap and has not lain flat since. He has paid a copper for the fare, a copper and a half for a loaf, a copper for a bowl and a copper for the loft. He sleeps in **the loft over the tap, up the keeper's stair**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:250:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and seventy-seventh day past the Line**, at Lowmarch. Days on the page: 271, 272, 273, 275, 276, 277; Vastin's window, 265–276. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:266:**Vastin.** No office, no seal, no rank; he left the seal in a tray "some months" ago and walked three hundred miles. **No age is stated.** A bad knee; raw hands; a left hand that will not lie flat. **No Iron Wall has been shown or named.** He has handed over three things in his own order and holds Karis's receipt in his coat. He has said: that he holds no office and has no sanction; that the layer cannot be opened ("There is no key"), on the authority of the office's own page; that the one line which should name its maker cites a title and sends its reader to Treswick's lower archive (his own copy of it); that nothing of his follows him and the Stair's rim is not his; that the pending paper is unchanged; why he did not take it to a council. He knows the six by name. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, Karis's case or the sites (beyond hearing Brom say "four on the hide" and Lira name the Stair), who held the abstracts, which classification event the sheet means, or what is under the bar. He has not weighed the sheet's date. He has not read the flat's last row through, and nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He was sent to bed, began to argue twice, took four stairs fast and the rest slowly; whether that was the order or the knee is not settled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:270:**Pike's book and the cloth.** **Eleven lines.** The season line's number still blank. **Eleventh on the new cloth**, painted on the 272nd. Vastin is "nothing yet" and is not entered. Oryn is on no slip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:292:**Movement 2 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the 24 coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed; the page made a copy; the layer cut to four facts (Lira and Brom say what it changes: there is nobody to ask); *Total* made the anomaly column's entry; the technician's sheet read out by Lira with a date and no figures, filed at and laid back at the end of the second row; Seln's stillness re-entered in a new order; receipt and night log made literally true ("Read in part. Understood in no part."); the completion report's five strokes and count of six; ch7's opening oriented. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling above borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (ice 111 days; the wrist 124; the sling 170; the rim 163; the cord 109; the report 175). Three fixes applied by the coordinator: ch7 "a healer's Path" → "a healer's craft" (no possessive before Path in narration); ch8's bluff memory cut back to what Book 5 shows; ch10 "through a frame shop" removed. Rulings from the recheck: **Lira reading the sheet aloud is the author's staging and stands** (the map protects the wording, the sum and the withholding, not the reader); the two descriptions of the cited record agree. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 30,105 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (11 protected). Purse 118 marks; deployment thirty; the night before day 278 at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:301:- **The cut (the author's staging stands; BOOK_MAP §8 allows it).** A hundred strides, a stride of ice down the middle, scree on the south, a low north bank, the sink fifty-five yards below it. Eight hounds (five seen, three hidden). The den had learned the road: it runs to where a declaration ENDS. Karis, Oryn and the mule were at the foot; Vastin, a stride behind Brom, stepped out and **declared Iron Wall** — a plane across the road from a line struck with his stick, wall to wall, two feet from Cael, rooted (he may not lift a foot), loud, spending him to the floor. Brom's rock (twice), Lira's knife with the left hand holding, Seln in the heap; five dead; **three went through the rotten ice of the sink and did not come up**. Costs: Brom's right foot (two toes, ten days from the 279th); **Vastin's right knee** (four holes shut by Oryn after "May I?" / "Yes"; the joint bound with laths; **a month** from the 279th: stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall). Karis's sixth line: *It goes to where a declaration ends, if it has learned that the declaring moves.* Twenty paid; **purse 138**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:304:- **The date.** Seln drew the technician's sheet from the foot of the second row; the row counted a sheet short in Cael's hands; Seln set the sheet before him without a word. **Cael read the date and knew it for the day of his own Kindling** (the first line of his file). Only Cael and Seln know; neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. Karis knows both have read the sheet. **No figures are printed, no span is computed, and there is NO second calendar** (the author's stations'-year offset was cut: the series calendar is the owner's). The sheet lies again at the foot of the second row.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:326:- **Iron Wall as shown.** Named by Vastin (16:109); **no tier is stated**. He steps into the road and brings the stick's foot down once; a line runs from his boots across the cut and cracks the ice white; "the air stood up from it": a face from bank to bank as tall as the scree, seen only by the frost that lies on it. It holds eight hounds at a run. It does not go anywhere; **he may not lift a foot**; each blow on it comes down through him into the stiff leg; it goes out of him steadily; it shuts the road and not the banks. "A Path of the tribunal floor… taught for fields; and a field is ground where a thing has been declared, a hearing, or a square, or a gate with a crowd at it." "I have stood on eleven such."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:345:**Calendar.** A little before noon on the **two hundred and eighty-first day past the Line**, going down the western side of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. Days on the page: 278, 279, 280, 281. No season, month or weekday name; no figures for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:349:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments; no eleventh.** **Deployment thirty-two.** Left palm stung by Ember. He ruled on a job and has made no vow. **He has read the technician's date, laid it against the first line of his own file, and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. He has not written it, has told nobody, and has put no verb to it.** He said "You do now" to Vastin at the hold. He has written in the log, at Oryn's asking, that inside Treswick he does not go near the station. **He has laid his hand on the page once, on the rise, and Karis has it again.** He has seen the light on the crown and turned from it. He carries a box. He asked "Who's Cleon?" and has the name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:365:**Pike's book.** Eleven completed lines. The clearance is taken (five strokes and a healer's line) and not yet said closed; **the thumbed slip is in Brom's shirt**. The season line's number still blank. Eleventh on the cloth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:381:- **Knowledge:** Cael and Seln alone know that the unprinted date matches Cael's Kindling day; neither has said or written it, neither has interpreted the sequence, and neither knows for certain what the other concluded (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:3–31,59–65,85–149`). Karis knows both men have read the sheet but not what they made of it (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:143–149`). Vastin heard the records reading but does not know the arithmetic, integration mechanism or Cael's fragments (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:159–205`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:266`). Oryn heard the archive discussion from the basin but not the date conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-18.md:229–231`; `packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:56`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:382:- **Bodies:** Vastin's right knee is shut, lath-bound and on day two of Oryn's thirty-day month on the 281st; stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall, and he has finally accepted being priced equally (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:27–65`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:151–169`). Brom's right two toes are bound with eight days left on the ten-day term, and his right shoulder remains in the older healer's knot; he must put a load down if it speaks (`manuscript/chapter-16.md:75`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:131–139`). Lira's arm remains slow and is on day sixteen out of wool (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:119–129`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:397:- **Vastin and Cael at the three-mile post.** Vastin SAT for the first time since the cut, of his own choosing, where he could not rise without Cael's arm. "I read your file" (no span of years). Cael: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." (protected, Cael's). **Why he declined** (the author's, amended to locked Book 6): the case shown him at Ostrand is the true and causal reason — the office had shown him what it did with honest readings; and privately part of him was relieved never to learn what a plate would say (a second silence would have been turned on Cael; a plate that lit would have been turned on nine thousand of his own readings). A sound act, and glad of it for a bad reason. **What Cael gave him:** that the place has been read twice that day with "the one thing I've got that reads", and nothing came back because that thing only feels what moves. NOT what reads, nor fragments, the mechanism, the date. Vastin did not ask. "It is a place where two people can stand": ground, not friendship. The S7 log verbatim ("color" stands).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:400:- **Seln's report (the 282nd night):** the old town stands on a quarry cut from inside; the lower archive is behind one iron door in the undercroft beneath the registry's yard; a practitioner registered under historical studies has standing entry by the week and may have matter brought down; **"Rune Path. Bronze."**; one clerk keeps the provision's book, which has had one name in it; the form has a line for the matter, a line for its bearer (one), and **a line for hands, entered by count**. Protected: Karis "Four hands." / Seln "Four… By count." / Lira "Four hands," … "I've two." / Cael wrote: *Entered by count. That's the door.* The S8 close verbatim (Cael; Karis), with OWNER-pending #53 ("four years and a hearing") as Cael's rough spoken figure, never repeated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:401:- **Cleon at noon (the 283rd)**, at the cook-house against the second wall: he looked at one sheet from its foot upward. Protected: "Off floors," (Cleon) / "Fused. Grey. No join. Three of them. I copied every mark on all three. Fifty-two sheets," (Karis) / "Fifty-two sheets," (Cleon). His terms: not on a counter; all the sheets, in their places; they come down to him; no names (his is on the card and is not said aloud); **not a word of what she thinks they are until he has looked**; one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says; no other carried light and no fire of anybody's. He gave a buff-edged card for the 284th at the second bell. He never looked at Cael. He stopped a step late on the paving. **His Path has not been shown.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:425:- **Cleon, as seen.** Not tall; grey hair cut short and badly; a coat the colour of dust; round shoulders; square pale hands with the nails pared to the quick; red-rimmed wet eyes, which he keeps shut while he eats; a voice "like a hinge". He looks at a sheet from its foot upward. He eats at the counter's end by the yard door at noon and goes down within the hour. **Cael knows him for Cleon at the counter** (the name said at a spring) and reads it once, written, at the head of the card in Lira's hands on the 283rd; nobody says it aloud. Karis told him at the counter what the floors are (the protected line: fused, grey, no join; three of them; fifty-two sheets), so his questions after it are of method only (rubbed or drawn; what light; which edge north; how far apart). **His terms (mine, one amended by the audit):** not on a counter; all of them, not a choice; they come down to him and he does not come up; his card, written at the counter (the matter; its bearer, one; hands, a figure), good for the next day only, at the second bell; no names given or wanted; not a word of what she thinks they are until he has looked; **one lamp goes down with them, his, held where he says, and no other carried light or fire of anybody's** (a light already burning below is not excluded). He pushed her sheet back without touching it. He left by the street door and stopped a full stride beyond it for three breaths. **He never looked toward the yard.** The Path is not shown; only that he rests his eyes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:437:**Calendar.** The forenoon of the **two hundred and eighty-fourth day past the Line**, under Treswick, on the head of the stair inside the iron door. Days on the page: 281 (the rise's foot; the posts; the three-mile pull-in), 282 (the bridge; the outer gate; the district; the inn; the district's edge; Seln's report), 283 (the cook-house at noon; the route; the evening), 284 (the inn yard at dawn; the second bell; two gates; the lane; the cut; the yard; the clerk; the door). Oryn: the first gate at dusk on the 282nd and the morning of the 283rd; the second gate from the night of the 283rd to first light on the 284th. No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:449:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. He lifted the road's silence and said what a town puts in its place. He learned the quarry, the provision, the clerk and the practitioner from a porter, without going above the trough; went up once on the 283rd as a counted hand with lamp oil and found the two ways round; **is on no card** ("I should cost you the count"). He has said the practitioner's Path and tier. The case is on him, shut; not mentioned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:455:**Cleon.** Named by the narration in chapter 24 (at the counter, and in the tags of the protected exchange) and once in chapter 26; never said aloud by anybody in this movement; Cael has read the name on the card. Rune Path, Bronze, by Seln's report only. He has set terms, written a card, and pulled the iron to. He has taken no notice of Cael. He has been told what the floors are (fused, grey, no join; three; fifty-two sheets) and nothing of what the sheets are thought to mean.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:475:- **Vastin and Cael.** Vastin has confessed both the sound institutional reason for refusing certification and his private relief at not learning what another plate would say. Cael has given him the fact of two self-readings and the instrument's limit, but not what reads, fragments, mechanism, date or arithmetic. Each holds one fact from the other; the relationship is explicitly ground, not friendship (`ch21:121–223` after fix 4).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:486:- **Cleon.** Protected, all his: "I know that hand." (of the Hall's fourth sheet); "Being believed — … It's the end of being able to be wrong."; "Give me a week." (the 284th); "They're orders."; the two-part limit ("I can tell you these are orders. I can't tell you what they order…"; "It doesn't work on a river, and it doesn't work on a man, and it doesn't work on a tree… It costs me my eyes for an hour after and nothing else."); "Same make."; and the 287th close ("documentation… built the same way twice… never once slept well since."), in which he uses Karis's name (he heard Brom say it). Karis: "Older than [UNBOUND]." **His Path has been shown from OUTSIDE only**: he looks at a made thing from its foot upward, without blinking, and says which signs BEAR (white), which are CARRIED (black) and which are NOTHING (red, packing); his plank's four rows are the same lines as rows on the Hall's fourth, the Stair's ninth and twenty-first, and the Ring's sixth sheets. **On the 287th he set his own week to run from that day to the 293rd, with everything else put aside**; at its end every sheet goes up. The bundle on his shelf ("Paper. Not stone.", from the same shelf as the plank) is tied and unread. He has not noticed Cael, who holds his lamp ("a hand to the left"); he knows nothing of the alley, the fragments or the mechanism.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:489:- **Brom (the 286th)** righted a broker's dray off a lad's foot in the registry's yard with his back and **no Path opened**, wrenching the LEFT (good) shoulder; a broker's man offered a guard's post inside the second wall (a sealed monthly pass, a bed, the house's coat, four marks and found; "Ask for the factor."); "I'll think on it."; he took up his box on the bound RIGHT shoulder ("Cart was heavier"), and carries it there — **a debt Cael has entered, owed at the mill to two healers**. "You think Karis is right?…" / "Good. I'd hate to have turned down a real job for a wrong hunch." His two toes were done on the 289th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:495:- **Seln's finding (a finding, not a fact):** the six opened no Path because they cannot be written down in that town either; they wanted one of the crew to declare, a light shown for it to a watcher below, and a box carried off; they saw a wall and a rock and nothing of quiet ground or what Cael carries. **They know the loft and have shown that they know** (the watcher stood in the light of the painted door). Cael has ruled only that the cut is not climbed at dusk again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:499:All reads on Sol (gpt-5.6-sol): editorial; cold read; source-distance (1 tracked passage, ch27 scene 2; probe 2% / 14%); plan / canon / protected-text audit (RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES; ten exact fixes; all nineteen author flags and every minted item KEPT). Eight applied by the coordinator (five markers restored whole with speakers — two of Cleon's had been staged as Karis's — and three joins). Two DECLINED: the audit wanted the eleventh's lines printed as system text under a FRAGMENT ACQUIRED heading; the protected unit is Cael's own cataloguing (it names Vastin and says "Eleventh"; the twelfth says "me"), so the author's frame stands and the coordinator set the unit in italics instead of a code fence. **Repair r1 in progress with the same author.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:512:- **Cleon.** He missed his noon bowl on the 284th and has gone up for it on the other days. He does not touch paper with his skin: he points with a reed as long as a forearm. Three bowls of counters (white pebbles, black pebbles, red squares of broken tile). He does not blink while he looks; his eyes run; he rests them shut for an hour. To Cael at two feet the Path "made no sound at all". Brom said Karis's name in his hearing on the 286th ("I said no names." / "I never gave it to you. I gave it to her."). "It was the first thing I did when I came here": he has looked at the grey bridge twice. He made a sound "that was nearly a laugh" on the 290th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:515:- **Cleon's week (as repaired).** On the 284th, from his chair, with his eyes shut, Cleon said what being believed was to him (protected) and then asked for a week (protected: "Give me a week."); Karis asked the five for the same week in her own words ("I should like his week"), and Cael said that it was hers. On the 287th he re-set it: he had spent the half of the first on his own page, which he read every morning before he would look at hers; that is put by, and the week is his, from that day, with nothing else on the desk. At its end every sheet goes up and the clerk writes that it is gone (he will not have matter lying a month under *the same*). Its seventh day is the 293rd; three days are left after the 290th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:518:- **Brom's yard.** A broker's dray (two wheels as tall as Lira, one mule, a square of slate painted on its side) loaded with roofing slate shed its near wheel on the yard's slope; the slates slid and pinned the carter's lad by the boot against the dock's kerb. Brom stopped the yard-men's lever at the high side, took the low corner on his left shoulder with no grey, held while Lira drew the lad out by his belt, and was let down onto two split logs driven under the axle by Cael and a yard-man. The lad's five toes bend. **The broker's factor** (a good grey cloak, a broad hat, a shaved chin, clean hands, a tally; no name, no face): the house is the third on the brokers' street with the slate above its door; a guard's post at its store inside the second wall; a standing pass, sealed, by the month; a bed in the house above the wall; the house's coat; **four marks, and found**. His master "keeps eleven on his doors" who will not shift a keg until they have lit up, "and then it's a line in somebody's book". Brom: "I'd have taken it at sixteen and written home the same night."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:523:- **Seln's finding.** They opened no Path, though the one on the landing stood like a man who has one: a Path opened under that wall is entered by whoever sees it, and they took the same care as the six to have nothing of theirs entered. The bow was to make somebody open; the light was to tell somebody below. They went for a box and not for Brom: they were told to bring away what was carried. "What they would have been glad to find was on a roof above their heads." The four went two east and two west along the lane, hoods back before the first corner; the two below left by the carts' gate, which had been left on the latch for them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:530:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and ninetieth day past the Line**, in the long loft at Treswick. Days on the page: 284 (the Deepstacks), 285 (the hatch; the lamp), 286 (the dray; the board; Seln's roof at night), 287 (the morning log; the figures; four times; Cleon's week and close; the parapet), 288 (the test; ten letters; "We are looked at"), 289 (the loft paid; the ladders; thirteen), 290 (fourteen; the alley; the loft). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:534:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Eleven fragments. Deployment thirty-two.** He has stood unfiled in the middle gallery. He has been the lamp since the 285th and has knelt two feet from Rune in use for five days; nothing has come of that. He has begun to put the light where the looking will go. He wanted the Path tried on himself, wrote that he had not said so, and has not said so. He has the eleventh (Iron-Wall-adjacent), has read its lines, has told it no three times, and has not used it. **He has not told Vastin**, and holds that he cannot without telling the mechanism, which is the six's. He has not set foot on the square or its steps and has not looked at the crown; he has walked the lane with its four alleys fourteen times. He has ruled that the cut is not climbed at dusk again and has ruled nothing else for the morning. Body: sound; a tarred case struck his ear.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:546:**Cleon.** Rune Path, Bronze; shown from outside only. He has said that he knows the hand; has shown the board; has said what bears, what is carried and what is nothing; has given the limit in both its parts; has said what being believed is to him and asked for a week (the 284th); has re-set that week to run from the 287th with his own page put by; has spoken his close; has Karis's name and has used it once. **He has taken no notice of Cael.** He does not know that anybody was set upon in the cut.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:550:**The faction.** Six, hooded, unnamed, faceless. It reached inside the third wall, opened no Path, took nobody and nothing, and saw a wall, a rock, a knife in a stave and a boy standing on a step. **It saw nothing of what Cael carries.** It saw Vastin's face uncovered and an Iron Wall. It knows the loft, and has shown that it knows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:552:**Objects and money.** **134 marks** (136 less two for the loft's second week, paid on the 289th; the loft is theirs to the 295th). The reserve sealed in the third box. Three boxes, the kit case, the flat and the hide are in the loft. The fifty-two first copies are on Cleon's tables. In the loft besides: a shortened watchman's stave with a knife-cut in it; the card for the 291st. Two bolts were left lying in the cut. Still owed: sixty yards of four-strand to the Lowmarch ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:559:Packet 006 carries the 291st, borrowed handcart, Karis's bound left hand, eleven fragments, and the fact that three clerk questions remain unasked (`MOVEMENT-006.md:26–28`). Its author must additionally inherit the following surviving particulars:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:563:- **Cleon's knowledge and statements.** Cleon knows Karis's name and has used it once; he knows the hand, has externally demonstrated bearer/carried/ornament and “orders,” has stated both limits, has matched the same make, and has delivered the documentation/built-twice close. His week runs from the 287th through the 293rd. He has not noticed Cael, learned of the alley, shown the inside/lean, or acquired knowledge of the mechanism (`chapter-27.md:187–199`; `chapter-29.md:193–289`; `chapter-30.md:253–279`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:117`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:568:- **What the faction knows.** It knows the loft and has deliberately shown that knowledge. It saw Vastin's uncovered face and Iron Wall, plus a rock/knife/still boy, but no Path from another crew member, no face of its own was secured, and it saw nothing of quiet ground or Cael's fragments. Seln's finding is that it wanted a visible declaration and a carried box and avoided being entered itself (`chapter-33.md:247–289`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:121`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:569:- **Inn, purse, count and day.** Six are in the long loft over the stable; it is paid through the 295th, with pot at dusk and seven bowls. Purse 134, reserve sealed in the third box. The below-ground daily count remains Karis as bearer plus four hands; Seln is never one of them. Night of day 290 is complete; Movement 6 opens day 291. The cut will not be climbed at dusk again, but no further route ruling has been made (`chapter-31.md:265–267`; `chapter-33.md:277–305`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:101–103,123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:570:- **Lira and remaining objects.** Lira is day twenty-five out of wool, has a bruised right shoulder, and the left arm took nothing. Three boxes, kit case, flat and hide are in the loft; the 291st card is there; the shortened watchman's stave is with Seln; two plain bolts remain in the cut; sixty yards of four-strand are still owed and Brom means to buy them going out (`chapter-33.md:285–307`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:107,123`).

