    60	
    61	How the road east reads in reverse. The plank room's crowd. The meadow's details. Teague's crew at the table. How the grade's numbers come off the sheets. Millrace's lean-to, light and noise. How long the deep reading takes on the page.
    62	
    63	## Where we leave pressure
    64	
    65	Twelve walk east along a straightedge's line, two of them on no wall's count. A healer's route and a researcher's archive ride on one mule. A boy carries two findings that do not agree and a warning that has started to lean. Five days out is a fence the Compact built, and somebody is still watching it.

