editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:197:They came down the street with the brake on, which was Brom, walking backward into the hill. The roofs of the district went by on the left hand, grey, with their smoke going up straight. Cael looked at them. He had looked at them on every journey by that road, to keep his eyes off a wall; and he found, this evening, that he had no eyes to spare for a wall in any case.
