editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-39.md:205:In the lane the four alleys had lost their white. He pushed through four bars of a paler light, with a shoulder against his own at each; and he did not look at them, and he did not think about them. He looked at a pair of raw hands on a tarred case, a yard from his face.
