editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:21:Karis was not looking at the sheet any longer. She had turned, on the spot where she had been put, and her eyes were going down the gallery: over the Hall's twelve, and the long table with its three rows, and the Ring's eleven beyond. She looked at them as she had once looked at a bluff from six miles off, counting.
