--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md-30-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:31:Cael had the light there before it, and did not have to think of where. He had been looking where that man looked for six days together, a hand to the left of him, and had taken it for a groom's knowledge of a horse. The finger came to the fifth row, and went along the signs, the white and the three black and the red, without touching one of them, and slowed as it went.
