editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:259:He looked at the three strides. The old man slept in a stall now. The pallet by the gable had been rolled, and there was nothing between his knee and the blanket but boards. He could cross them. He could lift one corner of a horse-blanket, and see for himself whether the thing on the crown burned as it had always burned.
