editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-37.md:325:She was thin, and tall for her age, with her hair in one plait and a sheepskin on her shoulders that was too big. She was frightened, and she was trying to walk as though she were not. Oryn had a square face that showed little, and she kept it so; but she had looked for that walk, and it was there, as it always was. Every one of them came across the clay like a person carrying a full pail.
