./books/book-08-before-the-paths/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:97:**The people (minimal by design, per the series convention):** **Cleon** (above). **Vastin** — returning, independent (see the Series-fit note and the Bible). **Teague** and his crew — the rival independents from Book 7 `[B7-OK]`, come for the spring bearing-work as promised; still named-by-role beyond Teague; Force Path (Teague), Bronze by a registry he stopped reporting to. **Pike** — the Lowmarch board-keeper, the winter frame (Ch1) only. Unnamed by design: the faceless faction (the reach into Treswick; the road ambush), the Treswick registry clerk, the Deepstacks' absent staff, the Compact watch at the Sunken Span, the carters and the ferry-hands. No new fauna required; stillhounds and shale-backs recur as established, and quiet ground still dens stillhounds.
