editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-38.md:101:[[TIER-B: The leaf (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 1), read aloud once by Karis: "In the years of the unmaking, when the un-bound walked in the land and no wall stood against them and no law held, and the cities of the east were emptied and the cities of the west were emptied and the rivers ran wrong" … "there came one who saw the shape of it, and set himself to the ordering. And he made the measure, and the seat, and the tier, and the mark that is given at the kindling, that each should know what he is and none should be what he is not. And he set the apparatus over all the land, and the land was ordered, and the un-bound came no more." / "And the" [the scraped name: four or five letters' width, the first upright stroke showing] "— set the apparatus over all the land, that the un-bound should not come again, who had near unmade the world before the ordering of it. And this is the reason of the apparatus, and this is all of its reason, and let none who come after forget it, though the un-bound be forgotten: that they should not come again." — the plan gives the unit with an elision in its first sentence and a bracketed place for the scraped name; staged as Karis's one reading, standing at Cleon's desk under the fixed lamp, her finger an inch above the skin, with Cleon two paces back with his eyes shut, Cael at the desk's left side and Vastin on a box six strides off; the object (horn-coloured, point-written, the scraped place with its one upright stroke) is described before this line and is not described again; coordinator to supply protected text]]
