9:- **Counts and money pass.** Movement 5 closes with eleven fragments, deployment thirty-two and 134 marks (`STATE_LEDGER.md:534,552`). The 291st log carries 134 and thirty-two (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:15`); the twelfth is catalogued once and remains deployment none (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:279`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:225`); the dinner spends four and leaves 130 (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:141–143,219`); the 293rd log still says deployment thirty-two and 130 (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:269`). The eleventh remains undeployed and Vastin remains untold (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:157–163`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:27`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:225`), matching the closed state (`STATE_LEDGER.md:534`).
10:- **People and bodies pass.** Karis enters with fourteen letters and a bound left hand (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:41,273`), reaches seventeen on the 291st (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:105–127`), twenty-one on the 292nd (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:49–67,127`) and twenty-three on the 293rd (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:249`); the closed entry is fourteen letters and seven stitches in the left palm (`STATE_LEDGER.md:486,536`). Vastin's right knee is carried, ridden, lowered on his seat and kept from kneeling or wall-work (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:5–23,71–95,221–229`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:53–113`), consistent with the re-lathed knee on day eleven at the Movement 5 close (`STATE_LEDGER.md:538`). Brom moves the handcart by leaning at the hips, not lifting either arm above the elbow (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:71–79`), consistent with both damaged shoulders (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30`). Lira is twenty-seven days out of wool on the 292nd and uses the arm within the established slow range (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:281–285`; `BOOK_MAP.md:249`).
11:- **Deepstacks and custody pass.** The cart party remains Karis as bearer plus four counted hands; Seln stays above (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:43–57,83–105,185–217`). The iron door, twenty-seven steps, three galleries, fifty-two sheets, tall eastern ledgers, fixed lamp, shelf bundle, black-oak plank and three boxes remain in their closed positions (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:209–305`; `manuscript/chapter-35.md:3–7`; `manuscript/chapter-38.md:3–43`), agreeing with `STATE_LEDGER.md:512–552`. Cleon's week remains the 287th–293rd (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:5`); his declared one-day overrun places the list of parts on the 294th (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–125`), exactly matching `BOOK_MAP.md:233–234` and `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28–37`.
12:- **Faction state passes.** The watcher is faceless, unnamed, takes nobody and is followed only as far as a gate Cael cannot lawfully cross (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:115–123,285–345`). Seln's conclusion is patience, not identity or headquarters (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:351–367`). This preserves the closed state that the faction knows the loft and has seen a porter/Wall but nothing of the fragments (`STATE_LEDGER.md:550,568`).
13:- **The route and writing pass.** The beam-man reads and writes the practitioner's name at the head of Cleon's card, not any restricted name (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:141–159`). This is the first thing of theirs entered against any name inside the third wall, but the card and the Movement 4 weigh-beam rule expressly authorize that ownership entry (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:7`; `packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:43–46`). It does not contradict “the clerk has not asked three things”: the beam-man is a different official, and the hatch clerk still chooses the form's count-only fields (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:185–203`). No restricted name is written at a gate, in the green book, on the parcel, or on the courier's slip (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:83–105,185–203`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:73–95`).
14:- **Knowledge passes, with one necessary exception stated precisely.** Cleon is the first outsider told how one fragment came: Cael tells him that pieces arrive near earnest Path use, that there were eleven before that day, and that the twelfth came from Cleon's demonstrated lean (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:197–203`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:27,45–53`). Thus “nobody outside the six knows” survives only as “nobody outside the six except Cleon knows any acquisition mechanism, and Cleon knows this one instance only.” Vastin knows neither the eleventh, the twelfth nor the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:157–163`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:27`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:255–263`). Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln know of the twelfth; Oryn and Vastin do not yet (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:131–171`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:43–63`).
18:1. **The twelfth turns unbidden before Movement 7.** The manuscript makes it incline or come round autonomously in the chamber (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:49,71,83,91,147,187`), at the rope-walk (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:193–199,375`), at the bridge/handcart (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:3–13`), at the dividers and table (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:109–123,157–173`), in the inventory (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:225`) and at the leaf (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:53–55`). This contradicts the M6 lock “It does not turn unbidden until Millrace” (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:69`) and spends M7's explicit first inward turn early (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43`). Fixes 18–36 preserve three deliberate, uncounted practice reads—rope-walk, dividers, inn table—while leaving the bridge, handcart, stair and leaf unread. No practice is a deployment; the total remains thirty-two under the edition's established trial/practice rule (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:98`).
19:2. **The light is made too explicitly agent-like.** The comparison to a Kindling plate which “attend[s]” to Cael and is “of the same kind” (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:251`) contradicts “deniable; nothing hints at agency” (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:70`). Fix 37 retains the required phrase “the particular weight of an instrument turning toward him” but removes the agency assertion. Cael still does not cross, lift the blanket or look again (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:257–267`); Lira sees only the log and closes the gap without looking outside (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:275–285`).
27:The required order is intact: daylight carts' street and honest beam (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:27–217`); Cleon's inside demonstration, acquisition, Lira-first telling, Cleon telling, warning, notice and stair cost (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:3–339`); the night tail (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:69–379`); the 292nd decipherment, parcel, dinner, inventory, light and Oryn cutaway (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:3–375`); the 293rd leaf, chronicle, stopped reach and copy (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:3–287`); Vastin alone, the stair, right-way-up lock and Seln on the street (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:3–221`); then Lira first, the fixed fire order, and the unlogged pole-two ending (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:3–293`). This matches the packet's consequential turns (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:52–61`) and scene order (`state/movement-006/EVENT-LIST.md:40–90`).
29:The withheld truths remain withheld except for the two repair findings above: nobody joins leaf to lamps/sigils/Arbiters/plates/stations; the deep-layer date is absent; the chronicle hole is unglossed; the eleventh is not told to Vastin; the twelfth is never used on a person or Cael's still place; the record's fear is reported and challenged rather than endorsed (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:179–217`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:57–85`; `packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:64–71`).
