99:1. **Leaf once.** After fix 6 it is read aloud once, by Karis, on the 293rd morning (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:95–105`; `BOOK_MAP.md:333`). Later sentences that closely paraphrase or interpret it are: Vastin's “another matter” / *Aimed* inference (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:23–29`); Lira's existence conclusion and Cael's clerk/breaking gloss (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:37,43–45`); Brom's country/children/one-sort price, fear, reason and rejected-verdict sequence (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:61–73`); Seln's restored registry/office purpose (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:101` after fix 11); Cleon's made/old account (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:115–119`); Vastin's aimed/category/person conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:135` after fix 12); and Cael's built/no-room conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:187` after fix 14). None quotes a run of the record's wording; all are packet-required reactions (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:58`). Karis stops Brom's proposed floor inference (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–85`).
100:2. **“Four hundred years.”** Current occurrences: Karis's fixed paraphrase at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:135` and the pole-two marker at `manuscript/chapter-40.md:187`. After fix 14 there are still exactly two, both fixed positions (`BOOK_MAP.md:334`).
101:3. **“The Architect.”** Current occurrences are the prose title at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:129` and inside the marker at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:133`. Fix 17 removes the first while fix 7 restores the complete title sentence, leaving one historical-title occurrence. It is never an agent or present-tense actor (`BOOK_MAP.md:335`).
102:4. **Chronicle hole.** The line stops at the hole; the narration calls no cause beyond worm or damp and supplies no missing words, theory or second source (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:163–193`). PASS against `BOOK_MAP.md:336`.
103:5. **“un-bound” / `[UNBOUND]`.** Current occurrences are four inside the leaf marker (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:101`), once in Karis's historical-kind paraphrase (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:139`), and once in her protected copy (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:237`). There is no `unbound` or `[UNBOUND]` in chapters 34–40. Fix 6 preserves four record uses. Every use means the record's historical kind, not a living label (`BOOK_MAP.md:337`).
104:6. **Two pages, no line.** No dialogue, narration or interior joins the leaf to the lamps finding, sigils, Arbiters, plates or stations (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:199–217`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:37–43`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–85`). *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* occur zero times. Vastin's sentence stops in the chamber and remains stopped in his cutaway (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:197–217`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:37–43,83–87`). Fix 37 also removes the light's unrelated plate analogy.
105:7. **Deep-layer date.** It is neither said, written, interpreted nor connected to the leaf anywhere in chapters 34–40. Cael's private omitted “one other thing” remains contentless (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:21–23`), preserving Cael/Seln-only knowledge (`BOOK_MAP.md:339`).
111:1. **Carts' street/weigh-beam — KEEP.** Honest practitioner-card ownership; no restricted name (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:121–181`).
112:2. **Handcart — KEEP.** Borrowed on an explicit return term and used within Brom's injury limits (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:33–39,71–81`).
113:3. **Vastin from the 291st — KEEP.** Stall, rope, cart and stair-seat solve the packet's mobility question without healing the knee (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:3–23,71–95,221–229`).
114:4. **Three unasked things — KEEP.** They explain rather than change the packet fact; the clerk still writes only *The same* and *four* (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:185–203`).
115:5. **Cleon learns only the hand injury — KEEP.** “Which lays?” never opens the alley or faction information (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:209–217`).
116:6. **Rune from inside — AMEND.** Keep *goes / sits / bears / nothing*, word breaks and light position (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:39–75`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:111,159`), but remove all unbidden turning. Fixes 18–36.
117:7. **Decipherment (*and*, *set*) — KEEP.** It does not pre-empt the 298th grade or list of parts, and nobody makes *set* a leaf-carving inference (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:49–67`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:37–43`).
118:8. **Telling rationale — KEEP.** It properly distinguishes Cleon's continuing craft from Vastin's held eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:153–173`).
