136:No unplanned named person, place or animal appears. The new people remain role-only: beam-man, watchmen, gate keepers, carrier, hold's old woman, hold child, her brother, red-capped girl and laughing boy (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:139–175`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:137–143,291–327`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:73–87,291–353`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:33–35`). Existing names and places—Cleon, Hesk, Denvash, Ardenmere, Reydan, Daeva, Ephram, Ternhall, Ostrand, Velmere, Treswick—are all inherited from the plan or closed text (`BOOK_MAP.md:480` onward; `STATE_LEDGER.md:534–552`).
142:- **Leaf audience and wording discipline.** Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin heard the record once; Lira, Brom and Seln read Karis's page; Oryn has not heard it (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:3–29,95–105,251–269`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:3–37,53–103`). Nobody who heard it quotes it. The surviving public reductions are *made*, *for a kind*, Lira's existence conclusion, Vastin's *aimed/category/person*, and Cael's built-to-prevent conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:179–189`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:37,135,187` after fixes 10, 12 and 14).
143:- **Fragments and knowledge.** Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two. The eleventh remains unused and known to Lira through the log but not Vastin. The twelfth is known to Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon; Oryn and Vastin have not been told. Cleon knows how this one fragment came but no other acquisition history. The warning is known only to Cael and Cleon and is in no book (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:197–239,279–339`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:15–63`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:219–227`). After repair, the only post-acquisition Rune reads are three deliberate practice reads and none is counted; the first unbidden turn remains M7 (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:193–199`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:109–173`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43`).
144:- **Cleon.** He has shown the Path's inside, been told the twelfth's mechanism, declined a dangerous sentence, given the warning, deliberately looked away for two days, promised the leaf stays under his hand and above no counter, and said “Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts.” (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:15–239`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:115–125,227–239`). He let the fifty-two sheets lie one extra night and has written the 294th card (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–125`).
145:- **Object positions at night on the 293rd.** The original skin leaf is between its beech boards under Cleon's jar at his desk; the paper chronicle remains under the registry with its hole slipped/marked; the shelf bundle is untied and the leaf's back/list is unread (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:31–43,163–193`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:137`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:289`). Karis's fair copy is in Cael's hand/coat after Seln returns it; Karis retains the second copy in her notebook (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:123–127`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:249–251`). The fifty-two sheets lie on their three tables one night more, and the black-oak plank remains against the third table (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–121`; inherited location `STATE_LEDGER.md:552`). The three boxes, flat and hide are back in the loft; the bearing is on the calfskin in the second box, the reserve stays sealed in the third, and Cael sits against the third (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:267–289`). Vastin and the tarred kit case are in the end stall (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:253–265`).
146:- **Bodies.** Vastin's right knee is day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd, still slat-bound, with stick/no kneeling/no running/no Wall; he sleeps in the end stall and can take only the inner stair on his seat/hands (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:53–113`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:253–263`). Karis's left palm remains stitched and bound; she writes right-handed but has begun to steady/use the left without noticing (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:227–247`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:249`). Brom still cannot raise either arm above the elbow; Lira is day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:71–79`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:281–285`).
147:- **Money, lodging and tools.** Purse 130; reserve sealed in the third box; loft/handcart through the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed. Hesk's dividers and note are shut in Hesk's book with Cael (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:95–99,141–143,267–273`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:267–289`).
148:- **Faction and route.** Last sighting: the altered boots pass the blue gate on the night of the 291st; no face, name or base learned, and Seln will not follow again. No watcher is on the kerb/doorways on the 293rd; Seln expects the road east watched (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:285–379`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:191–221`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:219–223`). Cael still will not cross the square/steps or take the dusk cut.
149:- **Seln and the case.** The case remains on him and shut; its contents remain unnamed. He has read the leaf copy and decided the case is worth keeping “a while longer” (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:91–105` after fix 11). His cache decision is not a declaration or disclosure.
150:- **Light and date.** Cael alone saw the unsteady line; Lira knows only the written claim and closed the blanket gap. The ruling is *hold* (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:239–285`). The deep-layer date remains known only and separately to Cael and Seln, unsaid and unwritten (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:21–23`; `BOOK_MAP.md:339`).
151:- **Reading orientation.** At the inner stair head Cael reads Karis's page right way up for the first time; M7 must preserve that change (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:143–163`; `BOOK_MAP.md:475`).
