+   old: `[[TIER-B: Cleon: "A record sits … An instruction *leans* … This is a stair." — the plan quotes this speech in three pieces with elisions (packet, "The reader (291st)"; BOOK_MAP §10 Tier C S13 gives the second and third pieces); staged as Cleon's, said to Karis while his eyes go between the open tally-book (a record of loads) and the Stair's ninth sheet laid beside it foot to foot, with Cael on one knee a hand to the left holding the lamp; coordinator to supply protected text]]`
+   new: `"A record," Cleon said, "sits. Every mark's where it is because a thing happened and somebody put the mark down after. You read it and the marks are *still*. They describe. Nothing in them wants anything." {{JOIN}} "An instruction *leans*. Every mark's where it is because a thing is meant to happen next, and the mark's pointing at the next thing. You put your attention on it and it's not still. It has a direction. It's built so that the eye goes *along* it, bearer to bearer, in an order, and you can feel the order as you can feel which way a stair goes in the dark by where the treads are. That's what I see. Not words. The lean."`
