+4. **Chronicle hole.** The line stops at the hole; the narration calls no cause beyond worm or damp and supplies no missing words, theory or second source (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:163–193`). PASS against `BOOK_MAP.md:336`.
+5. **“un-bound” / `[UNBOUND]`.** Current occurrences are four inside the leaf marker (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:101`), once in Karis's historical-kind paraphrase (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:139`), and once in her protected copy (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:237`). There is no `unbound` or `[UNBOUND]` in chapters 34–40. Fix 6 preserves four record uses. Every use means the record's historical kind, not a living label (`BOOK_MAP.md:337`).
+6. **Two pages, no line.** No dialogue, narration or interior joins the leaf to the lamps finding, sigils, Arbiters, plates or stations (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:199–217`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:37–43`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–85`). *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* occur zero times. Vastin's sentence stops in the chamber and remains stopped in his cutaway (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:197–217`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:37–43,83–87`). Fix 37 also removes the light's unrelated plate analogy.
+7. **Deep-layer date.** It is neither said, written, interpreted nor connected to the leaf anywhere in chapters 34–40. Cael's private omitted “one other thing” remains contentless (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:21–23`), preserving Cael/Seln-only knowledge (`BOOK_MAP.md:339`).
+
+## 6. New canon minted
+
+Every item in `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:116–137` is ruled below.
+
+1. **Carts' street/weigh-beam — KEEP.** Honest practitioner-card ownership; no restricted name (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:121–181`).
+2. **Handcart — KEEP.** Borrowed on an explicit return term and used within Brom's injury limits (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:33–39,71–81`).
+3. **Vastin from the 291st — KEEP.** Stall, rope, cart and stair-seat solve the packet's mobility question without healing the knee (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:3–23,71–95,221–229`).
+4. **Three unasked things — KEEP.** They explain rather than change the packet fact; the clerk still writes only *The same* and *four* (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:185–203`).
+5. **Cleon learns only the hand injury — KEEP.** “Which lays?” never opens the alley or faction information (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:209–217`).
+6. **Rune from inside — AMEND.** Keep *goes / sits / bears / nothing*, word breaks and light position (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:39–75`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:111,159`), but remove all unbidden turning. Fixes 18–36.
+7. **Decipherment (*and*, *set*) — KEEP.** It does not pre-empt the 298th grade or list of parts, and nobody makes *set* a leaf-carving inference (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:49–67`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:37–43`).
+8. **Telling rationale — KEEP.** It properly distinguishes Cleon's continuing craft from Vastin's held eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:153–173`).
+9. **Cup of water — KEEP.** Character action only; no canon collision (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:221–239`).
+10. **Cleon's looking-away — KEEP.** It is the packet-required covenant and remains out of the log (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:233–239,289–339`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:227–235`).
+11. **Tail route — KEEP.** The route is author-owned and learns only access/patience, not identity or base (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:95–367`; `packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:55,75`).
+12. **Parcel — KEEP.** Role-addressed through an established carrier chain; no restricted name is written or read at a counter (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:73–99`).
+13. **Meal — KEEP.** Four marks, two kept cups, purse 130 (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:135–181`).
+14. **Seln's slip — KEEP.** “Closed” only; source detail remains unimported (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:183–191`).
+15. **Light — AMEND.** Keep the visual event, inventory position, denial and Lira's blanket action; remove agency comparison with fix 37 (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:239–285`).
+16. **Oryn's fourth gate — KEEP.** Canon permits a device-free involuntary Kindling; roles and hold remain unnamed (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:289–375`; `universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md:19–25`; `editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/manuscript/chapter-03.md:81`).
+17. **Leaf object — KEEP.** Physical details do not contradict later packets and the back remains unread (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:31–59,225–249`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30,37`).
+18. **Who heard the leaf — KEEP.** The edition's staging fulfills Lira-first-at-fire (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:3–29,251–269`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:3–37`).
+19. **Page right way up — KEEP.** It pays §13 at the inner stair head without moving the 297th confirmation (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:143–163`; `BOOK_MAP.md:475`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:39`).
+20. **Cleon's day over — KEEP.** Required for the 294th list (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–125`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30,37`).
+21. **Yard fire staging — KEEP.** It preserves fixed speaker order, one above-ground Cleon appearance and the non-endorsement (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:223–275`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:3–245`).
+22. **Unnamed roles — KEEP.** No owner-supplied name is consumed (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:139–175`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:115–143,291–327`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:73–87,291–353`).
+
+## 7. Names
+
+No unplanned named person, place or animal appears. The new people remain role-only: beam-man, watchmen, gate keepers, carrier, hold's old woman, hold child, her brother, red-capped girl and laughing boy (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:139–175`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:137–143,291–327`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:73–87,291–353`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:33–35`). Existing names and places—Cleon, Hesk, Denvash, Ardenmere, Reydan, Daeva, Ephram, Ternhall, Ostrand, Velmere, Treswick—are all inherited from the plan or closed text (`BOOK_MAP.md:480` onward; `STATE_LEDGER.md:534–552`).
+
+## 8. Next-movement inheritance not already carried by MOVEMENT-007
+
+Movement 7 already carries the 294th, all-day list, twelve fragments, Karis's bound hand, Vastin day fifteen and no mule (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28–30`). Its author must additionally inherit:
+
+- **Leaf audience and wording discipline.** Karis, Cleon, Cael and Vastin heard the record once; Lira, Brom and Seln read Karis's page; Oryn has not heard it (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:3–29,95–105,251–269`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:3–37,53–103`). Nobody who heard it quotes it. The surviving public reductions are *made*, *for a kind*, Lira's existence conclusion, Vastin's *aimed/category/person*, and Cael's built-to-prevent conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:179–189`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:37,135,187` after fixes 10, 12 and 14).
+- **Fragments and knowledge.** Twelve fragments; deployment thirty-two. The eleventh remains unused and known to Lira through the log but not Vastin. The twelfth is known to Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln and Cleon; Oryn and Vastin have not been told. Cleon knows how this one fragment came but no other acquisition history. The warning is known only to Cael and Cleon and is in no book (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:197–239,279–339`; `manuscript/chapter-36.md:15–63`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:219–227`). After repair, the only post-acquisition Rune reads are three deliberate practice reads and none is counted; the first unbidden turn remains M7 (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:193–199`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:109–173`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43`).
+- **Cleon.** He has shown the Path's inside, been told the twelfth's mechanism, declined a dangerous sentence, given the warning, deliberately looked away for two days, promised the leaf stays under his hand and above no counter, and said “Tomorrow the rest of the leaf. The list of parts.” (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:15–239`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:115–125,227–239`). He let the fifty-two sheets lie one extra night and has written the 294th card (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–125`).
+- **Object positions at night on the 293rd.** The original skin leaf is between its beech boards under Cleon's jar at his desk; the paper chronicle remains under the registry with its hole slipped/marked; the shelf bundle is untied and the leaf's back/list is unread (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:31–43,163–193`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:137`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:289`). Karis's fair copy is in Cael's hand/coat after Seln returns it; Karis retains the second copy in her notebook (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:123–127`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:249–251`). The fifty-two sheets lie on their three tables one night more, and the black-oak plank remains against the third table (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:117–121`; inherited location `STATE_LEDGER.md:552`). The three boxes, flat and hide are back in the loft; the bearing is on the calfskin in the second box, the reserve stays sealed in the third, and Cael sits against the third (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:267–289`). Vastin is in the end stall; the tarred kit case is last explicit in his hands on the returning cart, and the prose does not state whether it finishes in the stall or loft (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:173–205`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:253–265`). M7 must not silently choose a different custody if the case matters.
+- **Bodies.** Vastin's right knee is day fourteen of thirty on the 293rd, still slat-bound, with stick/no kneeling/no running/no Wall; he sleeps in the end stall and can take only the inner stair on his seat/hands (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:53–113`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:253–263`). Karis's left palm remains stitched and bound; she writes right-handed but has begun to steady/use the left without noticing (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:227–247`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:249`). Brom still cannot raise either arm above the elbow; Lira is day twenty-eight out of wool on the 293rd (`manuscript/chapter-34.md:71–79`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:281–285`).
+- **Money, lodging and tools.** Purse 130; reserve sealed in the third box; loft/handcart through the 295th; sixty yards of four-strand still owed. Hesk's dividers and note are shut in Hesk's book with Cael (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:95–99,141–143,267–273`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:267–289`).
+- **Faction and route.** Last sighting: the altered boots pass the blue gate on the night of the 291st; no face, name or base learned, and Seln will not follow again. No watcher is on the kerb/doorways on the 293rd; Seln expects the road east watched (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:285–379`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:191–221`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:219–223`). Cael still will not cross the square/steps or take the dusk cut.
+- **Seln and the case.** The case remains on him and shut; its contents remain unnamed. He has read the leaf copy and decided the case is worth keeping “a while longer” (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:91–105` after fix 11). His cache decision is not a declaration or disclosure.
+- **Light and date.** Cael alone saw the unsteady line; Lira knows only the written claim and closed the blanket gap. The ruling is *hold* (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:239–285`). The deep-layer date remains known only and separately to Cael and Seln, unsaid and unwritten (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:21–23`; `BOOK_MAP.md:339`).
+- **Reading orientation.** At the inner stair head Cael reads Karis's page right way up for the first time; M7 must preserve that change (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:143–163`; `BOOK_MAP.md:475`).
