+### BOOK_MAP §9, line by line
+
+1. **Leaf once.** After fix 6 it is read aloud once, by Karis, on the 293rd morning (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:95–105`; `BOOK_MAP.md:333`). Later sentences that closely paraphrase or interpret it are: Vastin's “another matter” / *Aimed* inference (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:23–29`); Lira's existence conclusion and Cael's clerk/breaking gloss (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:37,43–45`); Brom's country/children/one-sort price, fear, reason and rejected-verdict sequence (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:61–73`); Seln's restored registry/office purpose (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:101` after fix 11); Cleon's made/old account (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:115–119`); Vastin's aimed/category/person conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:135` after fix 12); and Cael's built/no-room conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:187` after fix 14). None quotes a run of the record's wording; all are packet-required reactions (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:58`). Karis stops Brom's proposed floor inference (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–85`).
+2. **“Four hundred years.”** Current occurrences: Karis's fixed paraphrase at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:135` and the pole-two marker at `manuscript/chapter-40.md:187`. After fix 14 there are still exactly two, both fixed positions (`BOOK_MAP.md:334`).
+3. **“The Architect.”** Current occurrences are the prose title at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:129` and inside the marker at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:133`. Fix 17 removes the first while fix 7 restores the complete title sentence, leaving one historical-title occurrence. It is never an agent or present-tense actor (`BOOK_MAP.md:335`).
+4. **Chronicle hole.** The line stops at the hole; the narration calls no cause beyond worm or damp and supplies no missing words, theory or second source (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:163–193`). PASS against `BOOK_MAP.md:336`.
+5. **“un-bound” / `[UNBOUND]`.** Current occurrences are four inside the leaf marker (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:101`), once in Karis's historical-kind paraphrase (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:139`), and once in her protected copy (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:237`). There is no `unbound` or `[UNBOUND]` in chapters 34–40. Fix 6 preserves four record uses. Every use means the record's historical kind, not a living label (`BOOK_MAP.md:337`).
+6. **Two pages, no line.** No dialogue, narration or interior joins the leaf to the lamps finding, sigils, Arbiters, plates or stations (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:199–217`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:37–43`; `manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–85`). *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* occur zero times. Vastin's sentence stops in the chamber and remains stopped in his cutaway (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:197–217`; `manuscript/chapter-39.md:37–43,83–87`). Fix 37 also removes the light's unrelated plate analogy.
+7. **Deep-layer date.** It is neither said, written, interpreted nor connected to the leaf anywhere in chapters 34–40. Cael's private omitted “one other thing” remains contentless (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:21–23`), preserving Cael/Seln-only knowledge (`BOOK_MAP.md:339`).
