+1. **Leaf once.** After fix 6 it is read aloud once, by Karis, on the 293rd morning (`manuscript/chapter-38.md:95–105`; `BOOK_MAP.md:333`). Later sentences that closely paraphrase or interpret it are: Vastin's “another matter” / *Aimed* inference (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:23–29`); Lira's existence conclusion and Cael's clerk/breaking gloss (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:37,43–45`); Brom's country/children/one-sort price, fear, reason and rejected-verdict sequence (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:61–73`); Seln's restored registry/office purpose (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:101` after fix 11); Cleon's made/old account (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:115–119`); Vastin's aimed/category/person conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:135` after fix 12); and Cael's built/no-room conclusion (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:187` after fix 14). None quotes a run of the record's wording; all are packet-required reactions (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:58`). Karis stops Brom's proposed floor inference (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:75–85`).
+2. **“Four hundred years.”** Current occurrences: Karis's fixed paraphrase at `manuscript/chapter-38.md:135` and the pole-two marker at `manuscript/chapter-40.md:187`. After fix 14 there are still exactly two, both fixed positions (`BOOK_MAP.md:334`).
