+18. `manuscript/chapter-35.md`
+   old: `There was a table under that sheet, with pegs in it. There was a ring of brass in his fingers, and a desk six strides off, and a stair of dark stone that somebody had laid. The new thing inclined toward each of them in turn, mildly, like a head coming round. He did not let it look. He had been given a pair of eyes that were not his, in a room that belonged to the man they came from, and he did not know yet what they cost.`
