+23. `manuscript/chapter-35.md`
+   old: `The desk's lamp burned at the far end, on its iron arm, as it had burned on the first morning; and for most of the way it showed him nothing but itself. The shelves went by on either hand as walls go by in a dream. The new thing leaned at every bay. He kept his eyes on the flame, and counted.`
