+24. `manuscript/chapter-36.md`
+   old: `He glanced along the shed, to judge how much of it was left; he only meant to measure. But it was three hundred yards of a thing that somebody had built to go in one direction, with every post and plank and peg of it laid toward the far end; and the new thing behind his eyes came round to that as a weathercock comes round, before he had told it anything.`
+   new: `He glanced along the shed, to judge how much of it was left; he only meant to measure. But it was three hundred yards of a thing that somebody had built to go in one direction, with every post and plank and peg of it laid toward the far end; and, for one blink, he chose the new thing instead of his own eyes.`
